msgid "*Figure 3. Key Encapsulation Mechanism*\n"
msgstr "*Gambar 3. Mekanisme Enkapsulasi Kunci*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Digital signatures with asymmetric key cryptography {#digital-signatures-"
"with-asymmetric-key-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Tanda tangan digital dengan kriptografi kunci asimetris {#digital-"
"signatures-with-asymmetric-key-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[*Digital "
"signatures*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191)"
" are another powerful application of asymmetric key cryptography. They "
"provide authentication, integrity, and nonrepudiation enabled by the fact "
"that within AKC, entities possess unique private keys. The basic idea "
"underlying signature protocols is that senders of secure messages will "
"additionally *digitally sign* the messages using their unique private key. "
"The receiver will then verify the digital signature using the public key of "
"the sender. Within AKC, digital signatures can be implemented by using "
"algorithms specifically designed for that purpose or by using generic "
"cryptosystems.\n"
msgstr ""
"[*Tanda tangan "
"digital*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191)"
" adalah aplikasi lain yang kuat dari kriptografi kunci asimetris. Mereka "
"memberikan autentikasi, integritas, dan non-repudiation yang dimungkinkan "
"oleh fakta bahwa dalam AKC, entitas memiliki kunci privat yang unik. Ide "
"dasar yang mendasari protokol tanda tangan adalah bahwa pengirim pesan aman "
"akan secara tambahan *menandatangani secara digital* pesan menggunakan kunci"
" privat unik mereka. Penerima kemudian akan memverifikasi tanda tangan "
"digital menggunakan kunci publik pengirim. Dalam AKC, tanda tangan digital "
"bisa diimplementasikan dengan menggunakan algoritma yang dirancang khusus "
"untuk tujuan tersebut atau dengan menggunakan kriptosistem generik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 4. Digital signatures with asymmetric key "
"cryptography](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography/dig_sig_akc.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 4. Digital signatures with asymmetric key "
"cryptography](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography/dig_sig_akc.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 4. Digital signatures  with asymmetric key cryptography*\n"
msgstr "*Gambar 4. Tanda tangan digital dengan kriptografi kunci asimetris*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dedicated digital signature algorithms {#dedicated-digital-signature-"
"algorithms}"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma tanda tangan digital yang didedikasikan {#dedicated-digital-"
"signature-algorithms}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Currently, the US Federal Information Processing Standard (FIPS) for digital"
" signatures is a dedicated scheme simply titled the [*Digital Signature "
"Algorithm*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA). Somewhat similarly to the Diffie-Hellman protocol, the DSA uses the "
"algebraic properties of the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modular "
"exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is raised to a power "
"(exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For example $x^e mod m$ "
".\">modular exponential</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The set of integers modulo a prime number, where the group "
"operation is modular multiplication. Elements in the multiplicative group "
"are chosen in such a way that they are coprime to the modulus, ensuring that"
" each element has a unique multiplicative inverse within the "
"group.\">multiplicative inverses</DefinitionTooltip> for signature "
"generation and verification.\n"
msgstr ""
"Saat ini, Standar Pemrosesan Informasi Federal AS (FIPS) untuk tanda tangan "
"digital adalah skema khusus yang secara sederhana disebut [*Algoritma Tanda "
"Tangan "
"Digital*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA). Agak mirip dengan protokol Diffie-Hellman, DSA menggunakan sifat "
"aljabar dari <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Eksponensiasi modular adalah "
"sisa ketika sebuah bilangan bulat dipangkatkan (eksponen) lalu dibagi dengan"
" sebuah bilangan (modulus). Misalnya $x^e mod m$.\">eksponensiasi "
"modular</DefinitionTooltip> dan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Himpunan "
"bilangan bulat modulo bilangan prima, di mana operasi grup adalah perkalian "
"modular. Elemen dalam grup multiplikatif dipilih sedemikian rupa sehingga "
"mereka koprim terhadap modulus, memastikan bahwa setiap elemen memiliki "
"invers multiplikatif unik dalam grup.\">invers "
"multiplikatif</DefinitionTooltip> untuk pembuatan dan verifikasi tanda "
"tangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [elliptic curve digital signature "
"algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_Curve_Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1162097661)"
" (ECDSA) is an ECC variant of DSA, providing the same functionality but with"
" significantly shorter keys. This results in improved efficiency, making it "
"a popular choice for systems with [resource "
"constraints](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2881444).\n"
msgstr ""
"[Algoritma tanda tangan digital kurva "
"eliptik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_Curve_Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1162097661)"
" (ECDSA) adalah varian ECC dari DSA, menyediakan fungsionalitas yang sama "
"tapi dengan kunci yang jauh lebih pendek. Ini menghasilkan peningkatan "
"efisiensi, menjadikannya pilihan populer untuk sistem dengan [kendala sumber"
" daya](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2881444).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Both DSA and ECDSA will be illustrated in more detail later.\n"
msgstr "DSA dan ECDSA akan diilustrasikan lebih rinci nanti.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Digital signature schemes using generic cryptosystems {#digital-signature-"
"schemes-using-generic-cryptosystems}"
msgstr ""
"Skema tanda tangan digital menggunakan kriptosistem generik {#digital-"
"signature-schemes-using-generic-cryptosystems}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to dedicated algorithms, digital signatures can also be "
"generated using generic asymmetric cryptosystems, such as "
"[RSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_(cryptosystem)&oldid=1163962255).\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain algoritma yang didedikasikan, tanda tangan digital juga bisa dibuat "
"menggunakan kriptosistem asimetris generik, seperti "
"[RSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_(cryptosystem)&oldid=1163962255).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"RSA, which will be discussed in detail in a later section, also exploits "
"modular multiplicative inverses and <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modular "
"exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is raised to a power "
"(exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For example $x^e mod m$ "
".\">modular exponentiation</DefinitionTooltip> as fundamental operations but"
" combines them in a different sequence than DSA. In RSA, the signer "
"typically creates a hash of the message and then encrypts the hash with "
"their private key, creating the digital signature. Any party can then verify"
" this signature by decrypting it with the signer's public key and comparing "
"it with the hashed message.\n"
msgstr ""
"RSA, yang akan dibahas secara rinci di bagian selanjutnya, juga memanfaatkan"
" invers multiplikatif modular dan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Eksponensiasi modular adalah sisa ketika sebuah bilangan bulat "
"dipangkatkan (eksponen) lalu dibagi dengan sebuah bilangan (modulus). "
"Misalnya $x^e mod m$.\">eksponensiasi modular</DefinitionTooltip> sebagai "
"operasi dasar tapi menggabungkannya dalam urutan yang berbeda dari DSA. "
"Dalam RSA, penanda tangan biasanya membuat hash dari pesan lalu mengenkripsi"
" hash dengan kunci privatnya, menciptakan tanda tangan digital. Pihak mana "
"pun kemudian bisa memverifikasi tanda tangan ini dengan mendekripsinya "
"menggunakan kunci publik penanda tangan dan membandingkannya dengan pesan "
"yang di-hash.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applications of asymmetric key cryptography {#applications-of-asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Aplikasi kriptografi kunci asimetris {#applications-of-asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Asymmetric key "
"cryptography](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Public-"
"key_cryptography&oldid=1163952916) is <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Something that is present or found everywhere, or something "
"that is widespread and commonly "
"encountered.\">ubiquitous</DefinitionTooltip> in modern digital technology "
"applications. The basic functionalities of AKC described above form the "
"building blocks of many higher-level application protocols, including:\n"
msgstr ""
"[Kriptografi kunci "
"asimetris](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Public-"
"key_cryptography&oldid=1163952916) bersifat <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Sesuatu yang ada atau ditemukan di mana-mana, atau sesuatu yang"
" tersebar luas dan umum dijumpai.\">ubiquitous</DefinitionTooltip> dalam "
"aplikasi teknologi digital modern. Fungsionalitas dasar AKC yang dijelaskan "
"di atas membentuk blok bangunan banyak protokol aplikasi tingkat lebih "
"tinggi, termasuk:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Internet communication:** Secure communication over the internet, such as "
"HTTPS, relies heavily on asymmetric key cryptography. The Transport Layer "
"Security (TLS) and its predecessor, Secure Sockets Layer (SSL), use "
"asymmetric key cryptography during the initial handshake process to "
"establish a symmetric key, which is then used for the rest of the "
"communication session.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Komunikasi internet:** Komunikasi aman melalui internet, seperti HTTPS, "
"sangat bergantung pada kriptografi kunci asimetris. Transport Layer Security"
" (TLS) dan pendahulunya, Secure Sockets Layer (SSL), menggunakan kriptografi"
" kunci asimetris selama proses handshake awal untuk menetapkan kunci "
"simetris, yang kemudian digunakan untuk sisa sesi komunikasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Authentication:** Asymmetric key cryptography is used to create digital "
"signatures, allowing an entity to authenticate a digital document or message"
" as coming from a specific sender. This is used in many scenarios, from "
"verifying software updates to legally binding digital contracts.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Autentikasi:** Kriptografi kunci asimetris digunakan untuk membuat tanda "
"tangan digital, memungkinkan suatu entitas mengautentikasi dokumen atau "
"pesan digital sebagai berasal dari pengirim tertentu. Ini digunakan dalam "
"banyak skenario, dari memverifikasi pembaruan perangkat lunak hingga kontrak"
" digital yang mengikat secara hukum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Email encryption:** Email encryption protocols such as PGP (Pretty Good "
"Privacy) and its open-source alternative GPG (GNU Privacy Guard) use "
"asymmetric key cryptography to ensure that only the intended recipient can "
"read the email content.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Enkripsi email:** Protokol enkripsi email seperti PGP (Pretty Good "
"Privacy) dan alternatif open-source-nya GPG (GNU Privacy Guard) menggunakan "
"kriptografi kunci asimetris untuk memastikan bahwa hanya penerima yang "
"dituju yang bisa membaca isi email.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Secure shell (SSH):** SSH is a protocol for secure remote login and other "
"secure network services over an insecure network. It uses asymmetric key "
"cryptography to authenticate the server to the client and, optionally, the "
"client to the server.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Secure shell (SSH):** SSH adalah protokol untuk login jarak jauh yang aman"
" dan layanan jaringan aman lainnya melalui jaringan yang tidak aman. SSH "
"menggunakan kriptografi kunci asimetris untuk mengautentikasi server ke "
"klien dan, opsional, klien ke server.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**VPN (virtual private network):** Asymmetric key encryption is used to "
"establish secure connections in VPNs, ensuring secure communication over "
"public networks.\n"
msgstr ""
"**VPN (virtual private network):** Enkripsi kunci asimetris digunakan untuk "
"menetapkan koneksi aman dalam VPN, memastikan komunikasi aman melalui "
"jaringan publik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Blockchain and cryptocurrencies:** Blockchain technologies, including "
"Bitcoin and Ethereum, use asymmetric key cryptography. For example, the "
"ownership of Bitcoin is established through digital signatures using "
"asymmetric key cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Blockchain dan mata uang kripto:** Teknologi blockchain, termasuk Bitcoin "
"dan Ethereum, menggunakan kriptografi kunci asimetris. Misalnya, kepemilikan"
" Bitcoin ditetapkan melalui tanda tangan digital menggunakan kriptografi "
"kunci asimetris.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Certificate authorities:** Asymmetric key cryptography is used by "
"certificate authorities (CAs) to issue and sign digital certificates, which "
"are used in TLS communication, code signing, email encryption, and more. A "
"digital certificate binds a public key to a specific entity (for example, a "
"person or server).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Otoritas sertifikat:** Kriptografi kunci asimetris digunakan oleh otoritas"
" sertifikat (CA) untuk menerbitkan dan menandatangani sertifikat digital, "
"yang digunakan dalam komunikasi TLS, penandatanganan kode, enkripsi email, "
"dan lainnya. Sertifikat digital mengikat kunci publik ke entitas tertentu "
"(misalnya, seseorang atau server).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 5. Issuing and signing digital certificates using asymmetric key "
"cryptography](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography/ca_akc.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 5. Issuing and signing digital certificates using asymmetric key "
"cryptography](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography/ca_akc.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 5. Issuing and signing digital certificates using asymmetric key "
"cryptography*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Gambar 5. Menerbitkan dan menandatangani sertifikat digital menggunakan "
"kriptografi kunci asimetris*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Security of asymmetric key cryptography {#security-of-asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Keamanan kriptografi kunci asimetris {#security-of-asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Several cryptographic notions come together to enable secure asymmetric key "
"cryptography, including:\n"
msgstr ""
"Beberapa konsep kriptografi bersatu untuk mengaktifkan kriptografi kunci "
"asimetris yang aman, termasuk:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Private key secrecy**: The most basic security requirement of AKC is that "
"the private key remains secret. However, since the private key must be "
"mathematically linked to the public key, private key secrecy also requires "
"that it be computationally infeasible to derive the private key from "
"knowledge of the public key. Key generation schemes within AKC rely on "
"computationally hard mathematical problems to facilitate this requirement.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kerahasiaan kunci privat**: Persyaratan keamanan paling dasar dari AKC "
"adalah bahwa kunci privat tetap rahasia. Namun, karena kunci privat harus "
"terhubung secara matematis dengan kunci publik, kerahasiaan kunci privat "
"juga mengharuskan bahwa tidak mungkin secara komputasi untuk menurunkan "
"kunci privat dari pengetahuan kunci publik. Skema pembuatan kunci dalam AKC "
"mengandalkan masalah matematis yang sulit secara komputasi untuk "
"memfasilitasi persyaratan ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Trapdoor functionality** In AKC, the encryption and decryption operations "
"involve different complementary keys from a single-key pair. Ciphertext "
"generated by encryption using one of the keys (for example the public key) "
"must be inscrutable to third parties while being easily decryptable by the "
"holder of the complementary key (in this case the private key). In other "
"words, encryption should resemble a [*trapdoor one-way "
"function*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Trapdoor_function&oldid=1163913265)"
" such that third parties cannot invert the operation and recover the plain "
"text but the private key provides a secret *trapdoor* that enables easy "
"inversion. Popular AKC algorithms use modular exponentiation to set up "
"trapdoor one-way function behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Fungsionalitas trapdoor** Dalam AKC, operasi enkripsi dan dekripsi "
"melibatkan kunci komplementer yang berbeda dari satu pasangan kunci. "
"Ciphertext yang dihasilkan oleh enkripsi menggunakan salah satu kunci "
"(misalnya kunci publik) harus tidak terbaca oleh pihak ketiga sementara "
"mudah didekripsi oleh pemegang kunci komplementer (dalam hal ini kunci "
"privat). Dengan kata lain, enkripsi harus menyerupai sebuah [*fungsi satu "
"arah "
"trapdoor*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Trapdoor_function&oldid=1163913265)"
" sedemikian rupa sehingga pihak ketiga tidak bisa membalik operasi dan "
"memulihkan teks biasa tapi kunci privat menyediakan *trapdoor* rahasia yang "
"memungkinkan inversi yang mudah. Algoritma AKC populer menggunakan "
"eksponensiasi modular untuk menyiapkan perilaku fungsi satu arah trapdoor.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Randomness**: The key generation process should also exploit randomness to"
" ensure that keys are unpredictable, as any pattern or predictability in key"
" generation could be exploited by an attacker. Randomness is also used for "
"padding during encryption to generate semantically secure ciphertexts and "
"within digital signature schemes to produce unique signatures even when the "
"same message is signed multiple times. For this reason, the use of strong "
"random number generators is an important part of AKC.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Keacakan**: Proses pembuatan kunci juga harus memanfaatkan keacakan untuk "
"memastikan bahwa kunci tidak dapat diprediksi, karena pola atau "
"prediktabilitas apa pun dalam pembuatan kunci bisa dieksploitasi oleh "
"penyerang. Keacakan juga digunakan untuk padding selama enkripsi untuk "
"menghasilkan ciphertext yang aman secara semantis dan dalam skema tanda "
"tangan digital untuk menghasilkan tanda tangan unik bahkan ketika pesan yang"
" sama ditandatangani beberapa kali. Untuk alasan ini, penggunaan generator "
"angka acak yang kuat adalah bagian penting dari AKC.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Large key size**: As in the case of SKC, large key sizes ensure protection"
" against brute force attacks. However, since large key sizes also increase "
"the computational cost of the encryption and decryption process, an optimal "
"solution needs to balance security and efficiency considerations. The "
"following table shows typical key sizes for various asymmetric key "
"cryptography protocols and applications:\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ukuran kunci besar**: Seperti halnya SKC, ukuran kunci yang besar "
"memastikan perlindungan terhadap serangan brute force. Namun, karena ukuran "
"kunci yang besar juga meningkatkan biaya komputasi proses enkripsi dan "
"dekripsi, solusi optimal perlu menyeimbangkan pertimbangan keamanan dan "
"efisiensi. Tabel berikut menunjukkan ukuran kunci tipikal untuk berbagai "
"protokol dan aplikasi kriptografi kunci asimetris:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Protocol | Typical Key Sizes (in bits)         | Application                    |\n"
"|----------|-------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n"
"| RSA      | 1024 (deprecated), 2048, 3072, 4096 | Encryption, digital signatures |\n"
"| DSA      | 1024 (deprecated), 2048, 3072       | Digital signatures             |\n"
"| DH       | 2048, 3072, 4096                    | Key exchange                   |\n"
"| ECDH     | 224, 256, 384, 521                  | Key exchange                   |\n"
"| ECDSA    | 224, 256, 384, 521                  | Digital signatures             |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Protokol | Ukuran Kunci Tipikal (dalam bit)    | Aplikasi                       |\n"
"|----------|-------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n"
"| RSA      | 1024 (usang), 2048, 3072, 4096      | Enkripsi, tanda tangan digital |\n"
"| DSA      | 1024 (usang), 2048, 3072            | Tanda tangan digital           |\n"
"| DH       | 2048, 3072, 4096                    | Pertukaran kunci               |\n"
"| ECDH     | 224, 256, 384, 521                  | Pertukaran kunci               |\n"
"| ECDSA    | 224, 256, 384, 521                  | Tanda tangan digital           |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Public key infrastructure**: In AKC, the private keys must be kept secret "
"by the owners while the public keys are shared. There needs to be a secure "
"mechanism to manage and distribute these public keys between users. *Public "
"key infrastructure* (PKI) provides a way to do this using *digital "
"certificates*. A digital certificate provides proof of identity of the owner"
" of the public key and is issued by a trusted authority like a certificate "
"authority(which is part of a PKI). Hence, PKI plays an integral part in the "
"security of modern application using AKC by enabling large-scale key "
"management (by creating, managing, distributing and revoking digital "
"certificates).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Infrastruktur kunci publik**: Dalam AKC, kunci privat harus dijaga "
"kerahasiaannya oleh pemilik sementara kunci publik dibagikan. Harus ada "
"mekanisme aman untuk mengelola dan mendistribusikan kunci publik ini antar "
"pengguna. *Infrastruktur kunci publik* (PKI) menyediakan cara untuk "
"melakukan ini menggunakan *sertifikat digital*. Sertifikat digital "
"memberikan bukti identitas pemilik kunci publik dan diterbitkan oleh "
"otoritas tepercaya seperti otoritas sertifikat (yang merupakan bagian dari "
"PKI). Karenanya, PKI memainkan peran integral dalam keamanan aplikasi modern"
" yang menggunakan AKC dengan memungkinkan manajemen kunci berskala besar "
"(dengan membuat, mengelola, mendistribusikan, dan mencabut sertifikat "
"digital).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Security risks to asymmetric key cryptography {#security-risks-to-"
"asymmetric-key-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Risiko keamanan terhadap kriptografi kunci asimetris {#security-risks-to-"
"asymmetric-key-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As outlined in the above table, modern asymmetric key algorithms such as RSA"
" typically employ much larger key sizes than commonly used symmetric key "
"counterparts such as AES-128. Even the ECC-based protocols (ECDH and ECDSA) "
"that have smaller key sizes employ a minimum of at least 224 bits for keys. "
"This in turn implies that a brute force attack involving an exhaustive "
"search of the private key space to identify the correct key is "
"computationally intractable in the foreseeable future. This remains true "
"even if quantum computers were to be deployed for this task. Therefore, "
"attacks against AKC usually focus on exploiting other potential weaknesses "
"of specific cryptosystems. Some well-documented attack modes target:\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang diuraikan dalam tabel di atas, algoritma kunci asimetris modern"
" seperti RSA biasanya menggunakan ukuran kunci yang jauh lebih besar "
"daripada pasangan kunci simetris yang umum digunakan seperti AES-128. Bahkan"
" protokol berbasis ECC (ECDH dan ECDSA) yang memiliki ukuran kunci lebih "
"kecil menggunakan minimal setidaknya 224 bit untuk kunci. Ini pada "
"gilirannya menyiratkan bahwa serangan brute force yang melibatkan pencarian "
"menyeluruh di ruang kunci privat untuk mengidentifikasi kunci yang benar "
"tidak dapat dilakukan secara komputasi di masa mendatang. Ini tetap berlaku "
"bahkan jika komputer kuantum digunakan untuk tugas ini. Oleh karena itu, "
"serangan terhadap AKC biasanya berfokus pada mengeksploitasi kelemahan "
"potensial lain dari kriptosistem tertentu. Beberapa mode serangan yang "
"terdokumentasi dengan baik menargetkan:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Algorithmic weakness** by using sophisticated mathematical and "
"computational means to undermine the hardness assumptions used to formulate "
"asymmetric key algorithms. For example, the security of RSA is predicated on"
" the difficulty of factoring large prime numbers, and recent computational "
"advances have [enabled successful factoring of 829-bit RSA "
"keys](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_Factoring_Challenge&oldid=1163481797)."
" Therefore, 1024-bit RSA is currently deprecated. As will be discussed "
"later, the primary risk posed by quantum computers to AKC also falls into "
"this category.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kelemahan algoritmik** dengan menggunakan sarana matematis dan komputasi "
"yang canggih untuk melemahkan asumsi kekerasan yang digunakan untuk "
"merumuskan algoritma kunci asimetris. Misalnya, keamanan RSA didasarkan pada"
" kesulitan memfaktorkan bilangan prima besar, dan kemajuan komputasi terbaru"
" telah [memungkinkan faktorisasi kunci RSA 829-bit yang "
"berhasil](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_Factoring_Challenge&oldid=1163481797)."
" Oleh karena itu, RSA 1024-bit saat ini sudah usang. Seperti yang akan "
"dibahas nanti, risiko utama yang ditimbulkan komputer kuantum pada AKC juga "
"masuk dalam kategori ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Imperfect randomness**, which can lead to weakness in the key generation "
"process. For example, if the random number generator used to create the keys"
" is flawed and generates keys that are not truly random, an attacker might "
"be able to predict the keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Keacakan yang tidak sempurna**, yang dapat menyebabkan kelemahan dalam "
"proses pembuatan kunci. Misalnya, jika generator angka acak yang digunakan "
"untuk membuat kunci cacat dan menghasilkan kunci yang tidak benar-benar "
"acak, penyerang mungkin bisa memprediksi kunci tersebut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Implementation flaws** such as errors in the implementation of "
"cryptographic algorithms that inadvertently reveal information about the "
"keys. For example, incorrect padding can potentially reveal details about "
"keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Cacat implementasi** seperti kesalahan dalam implementasi algoritma "
"kriptografi yang secara tidak sengaja mengungkapkan informasi tentang kunci."
" Misalnya, padding yang salah berpotensi mengungkapkan detail tentang "
"kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Side channels** that refer to information leakage from the physical system"
" that performs the cryptography. Such leaks could be in the form of timing "
"information, power consumption, or even sound, which can be exploited in a "
"so-called [*side-channel "
"attack*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Side-"
"channel_attack&oldid=1162235564). For example, analyzing how long "
"cryptographic operations take to execute could reveal the number of '1's in "
"a binary key. This seemingly innocent leakage significantly narrows the "
"search space, unveiling potential solutions to problems that initially "
"seemed insurmountable.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Side channel** yang mengacu pada kebocoran informasi dari sistem fisik "
"yang menjalankan kriptografi. Kebocoran seperti itu bisa berupa informasi "
"waktu, konsumsi daya, atau bahkan suara, yang bisa dieksploitasi dalam apa "
"yang disebut [*serangan side-"
"channel*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Side-"
"channel_attack&oldid=1162235564). Misalnya, menganalisis berapa lama operasi"
" kriptografi membutuhkan waktu untuk dijalankan dapat mengungkapkan jumlah "
"'1' dalam kunci biner. Kebocoran yang tampaknya tidak berbahaya ini secara "
"signifikan mempersempit ruang pencarian, mengungkap solusi potensial untuk "
"masalah yang awalnya tampak tidak dapat diatasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key exchange** by intercepting keys while they are being exchanged, such "
"as within a [*man-in-the-middle* "
"attack](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Man-in-the-"
"middle_attack&oldid=1164741355) (MITM). The DH protocol is susceptible to "
"MITM attacks if additional authentication steps are not incorporated.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pertukaran kunci** dengan mencegat kunci saat sedang dipertukarkan, "
"seperti dalam serangan [*man-in-the-"
"middle*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Man-in-the-"
"middle_attack&oldid=1164741355) (MITM). Protokol DH rentan terhadap serangan"
" MITM jika langkah autentikasi tambahan tidak disertakan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key storage** by aiming to steal keys from poorly secured storage. This "
"includes physical attacks such as manipulation or theft of storage "
"devices.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Penyimpanan kunci** dengan bertujuan mencuri kunci dari penyimpanan yang "
"tidak aman. Ini termasuk serangan fisik seperti manipulasi atau pencurian "
"perangkat penyimpanan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Securing asymmetric key cryptosystems against the variety of attacks that "
"are possible is therefore a significant task involving mathematical, "
"hardware, software, logistical, and legal considerations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengamankan kriptosistem kunci asimetris dari berbagai serangan yang mungkin"
" terjadi adalah tugas yang signifikan yang melibatkan pertimbangan "
"matematis, perangkat keras, perangkat lunak, logistis, dan hukum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "RSA {#rsa}"
msgstr "RSA {#rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [RSA (Rivest-Shamir-"
"Adleman)](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/359340.359342) algorithm is one of "
"the first public key cryptosystems and is widely used for secure data "
"transmission. It is a versatile cryptosystem in that it provides the "
"necessary operations to enable encryption, decryption, digital signatures, "
"and key exchange within a common framework.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma [RSA (Rivest-Shamir-"
"Adleman)](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/359340.359342) adalah salah satu "
"kriptosistem kunci publik pertama dan banyak digunakan untuk transmisi data "
"yang aman. Ini adalah kriptosistem serbaguna karena menyediakan operasi yang"
" diperlukan untuk mengaktifkan enkripsi, dekripsi, tanda tangan digital, dan"
" pertukaran kunci dalam satu kerangka kerja yang umum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this section, we will illustrate asymmetric key cryptography (AKC) using "
"RSA through simple examples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di bagian ini, kita akan mengilustrasikan kriptografi kunci asimetris (AKC) "
"menggunakan RSA melalui contoh-contoh sederhana.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will use the standard scenario of two parties, Alice and Bob, who wish to"
" communicate securely using AKC.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan menggunakan skenario standar dua pihak, Alice dan Bob, yang ingin "
"berkomunikasi secara aman menggunakan AKC.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The RSA algorithm {#the-rsa-algorithm}"
msgstr "Algoritma RSA {#the-rsa-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The basic RSA algorithm involves four operations: key generation, key distribution, encryption, and decryption:\n"
"1. **Key generation:**\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma RSA dasar melibatkan empat operasi: pembuatan kunci, distribusi kunci, enkripsi, dan dekripsi:\n"
"1. **Pembuatan kunci:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Public and private keys are generated based on mathematical principles "
"around prime numbers, where calculating them is easy, but the reverse is "
"hard.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kunci publik dan privat dibuat berdasarkan prinsip matematis seputar "
"bilangan prima, di mana menghitungnya mudah, tapi kebalikannya sulit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We'll refer to these:\n"
"    - Public key: $(e, n)$\n"
"    - Private key: $(d, n)$\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kita akan menyebut ini:\n"
"    - Kunci publik: $(e, n)$\n"
"    - Kunci privat: $(d, n)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Note that $n$ is common to both public key and private key, and is known "
"as the modulus. We will need to use this later.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Perhatikan bahwa $n$ umum untuk kunci publik dan kunci privat, dan "
"dikenal sebagai modulus. Kita akan perlu menggunakan ini nanti.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical detail\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Detail matematika\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose two distinct prime numbers, $p$ and $q$.\n"
msgstr "Pilih dua bilangan prima yang berbeda, $p$ dan $q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "chosen at random (for security).\n"
msgstr "dipilih secara acak (untuk keamanan).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"They should be similar in magnitude, but differ in length by a few digits, "
"to make factoring harder.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mereka harus berukuran serupa, tapi berbeda panjangnya beberapa digit, untuk"
" mempersulit faktorisasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prime numbers can be efficiently chosen using a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"An algorithm to determine whether a given number is prime. This"
" is relatively easy computationally compared to factorization.\">primality "
"test</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilangan prima bisa dipilih secara efisien menggunakan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Algoritma untuk menentukan apakah suatu bilangan adalah prima. "
"Ini relatif mudah secara komputasi dibandingkan faktorisasi.\">uji "
"primalitas</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $n = p*q$.\n"
msgstr "Hitung $n = p*q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$n$ is the modulus for both the public and private keys.\n"
msgstr "$n$ adalah modulus untuk kunci publik dan privat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The totient is a number, or "
"numbers, that are not greater than the given number, and are relatively "
"prime to it, having no factors in common.\">totient</DefinitionTooltip> "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to "
"indicate Euler's totient.\"> $φ$ </DefinitionTooltip>$(n) = (p-1)*(q-1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hitung <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Totient adalah bilangan, atau "
"bilangan-bilangan, yang tidak lebih besar dari bilangan yang diberikan, dan "
"relatif prima terhadapnya, tidak memiliki faktor yang "
"sama.\">totient</DefinitionTooltip> <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Simbol "
"Yunani, phi, sering digunakan untuk menunjukkan totient "
"Euler.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n) = (p-1)*(q-1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The totient is meant to be kept secret and typically discarded after key "
"generation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Totient dimaksudkan untuk dijaga kerahasiaannya dan biasanya dibuang setelah"
" pembuatan kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose an integer $e$ such that $1 < e < $ <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to indicate Euler's "
"totient.\"> $φ$ </DefinitionTooltip> $(n)$ and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest positive whole number "
"that can divide two or more of the given whole "
"numbers\">$gcd$</DefinitionTooltip>$(e, $<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The"
" greek symbol, phi, often used to indicate Euler's "
"totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)) = 1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih bilangan bulat $e$ sedemikian sehingga $1 < e < $<DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Simbol Yunani, phi, sering digunakan untuk menunjukkan totient "
"Euler.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ dan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - bilangan bulat positif terbesar yang "
"dapat membagi dua atau lebih bilangan bulat yang "
"diberikan\">$gcd$</DefinitionTooltip>$(e, $<DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Simbol Yunani, phi, sering digunakan untuk menunjukkan totient "
"Euler.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)) = 1$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"that is, $e$ and <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, "
"often used to indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ "
"should be <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Two numbers that have a greatest "
"common divisor of 1. For example, 3 and 13 are coprime because only 1 can "
"divide both of them.\">coprime</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"yaitu, $e$ dan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Simbol Yunani, phi, sering "
"digunakan untuk menunjukkan totient Euler.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ "
"harus <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Dua bilangan yang memiliki pembagi "
"bersama terbesar 1. Misalnya, 3 dan 13 adalah koprim karena hanya 1 yang "
"dapat membagi keduanya.\">koprim</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This number $e$ forms the public key <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"number of times a number is multiplied by "
"itself.\">exponent</DefinitionTooltip> and is typically chosen as a small "
"number for computational efficiency.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilangan $e$ ini membentuk <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Berapa kali suatu"
" bilangan dikalikan dengan dirinya sendiri.\">eksponen</DefinitionTooltip> "
"kunci publik dan biasanya dipilih sebagai bilangan kecil untuk efisiensi "
"komputasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The prime number $65537 = 2^{16} + 1$ is often used.\n"
msgstr "Bilangan prima $65537 = 2^{16} + 1$ sering digunakan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute $d$ to satisfy the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Consistency, or "
"equivalence ie. all behaving in the same way.\">congruence "
"relation</DefinitionTooltip> $d*e ≡ 1 ($<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"modulus is the remainder left over after dividing by the value specified. "
"modulo is the operation of doing "
"this.\">$mod$</DefinitionTooltip><DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek "
"symbol, phi, often used to indicate Euler's "
"totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n))$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hitung $d$ untuk memenuhi <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Konsistensi, atau "
"kesetaraan yaitu semua berperilaku dengan cara yang sama.\">relasi "
"kongruensi</DefinitionTooltip> $d*e ≡ 1 ($<DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Modulus adalah sisa yang tersisa setelah dibagi dengan nilai "
"yang ditentukan. modulo adalah operasi untuk melakukan "
"ini.\">$mod$</DefinitionTooltip><DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Simbol "
"Yunani, phi, sering digunakan untuk menunjukkan totient "
"Euler.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n))$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '       - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, $d$ is the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Also known as "
"reciprocal, a number, which when multiplied by the number given, results in "
"a value of 1.\">multiplicative inverse</DefinitionTooltip> of $e$ modulo "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to "
"indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yaitu, $d$ adalah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Juga dikenal sebagai "
"resiprokal, sebuah bilangan, yang ketika dikalikan dengan bilangan yang "
"diberikan, menghasilkan nilai 1.\">invers multiplikatif</DefinitionTooltip> "
"dari $e$ modulo <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Simbol Yunani, phi, sering "
"digunakan untuk menunjukkan totient Euler.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '       - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is more efficiently computed using the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"An efficient way of calculating the greatest common divisor of "
"two whole numbers. It improves on the original Euclidean "
"algorithm.\">extended Euclidean algorithm</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini lebih efisien dihitung menggunakan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Cara "
"yang efisien untuk menghitung pembagi bersama terbesar dari dua bilangan "
"bulat. Ini meningkatkan algoritma Euclidean asli.\">algoritma Euclidean yang"
" diperluas</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '       - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This number $d$ is the private key <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"number of times a number is multiplied by "
"itself.\">exponent</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilangan $d$ ini adalah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Berapa kali suatu "
"bilangan dikalikan dengan dirinya sendiri.\">eksponen</DefinitionTooltip> "
"kunci privat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The public key consists of $(e, n)$, and the private key is $(d, n)$.\n"
msgstr "Kunci publik terdiri dari $(e, n)$, dan kunci privat adalah $(d, n)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"2. **Key distribution:**\n"
msgstr ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"2. **Distribusi kunci:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The public key $(e, n)$ is made public to those who may wish to send a "
"message\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci publik $(e, n)$ dipublikasikan ke mereka yang mungkin ingin mengirim "
"pesan\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The private key $(d, n)$ is kept secret.\n"
msgstr "Kunci privat $(d, n)$ dijaga kerahasiaannya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Encryption:**\n"
msgstr "**Enkripsi:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice wishes to send a message $M$ to Bob. In this case a simple integer\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice ingin mengirim pesan $M$ ke Bob. Dalam hal ini bilangan bulat "
"sederhana\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice uses Bob's public key $(e, n)$ to encrypt the message into ciphertext "
"$C$\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice menggunakan kunci publik Bob $(e, n)$ untuk mengenkripsi pesan menjadi"
" ciphertext $C$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical detail\">\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Detail matematika\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$M$ is an <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"We consider an integer in this "
"example as the simplest case. Any message can be converted into an integer "
"based representation.\">integer</DefinitionTooltip> $0 ≤ M < n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"$M$ adalah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Kita mempertimbangkan bilangan "
"bulat dalam contoh ini sebagai kasus paling sederhana. Pesan apa pun bisa "
"dikonversi menjadi representasi bilangan bulat.\">bilangan "
"bulat</DefinitionTooltip> $0 ≤ M < n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$C ≡ M^e (mod n)$, where $C$ is the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr "$C ≡ M^e (mod n)$, di mana $C$ adalah ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"4. **Decryption:**\n"
msgstr ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"4. **Dekripsi:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob receives the ciphertext $C$\n"
msgstr "Bob menerima ciphertext $C$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bob uses his private key $(d, n)$ to decrypt the message back into message "
"$M$\n"
msgstr ""
"Bob menggunakan kunci privatnya $(d, n)$ untuk mendekripsi pesan kembali "
"menjadi pesan $M$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$M ≡ C^d (mod n)$.\n"
msgstr "$M ≡ C^d (mod n)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"This is the basic outline of RSA. In practice, [more sophisticated padding schemes](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577) are applied to the plain text $M$ before encryption to ensure that equal plain texts result in different ciphertexts. This prevents a range of possible attacks against naive implementations of RSA and enables <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"With only the ciphertext, and any relevant public information (such as public key for asymmetric key cryptography), and adversary cannot retrieve even partial information from the plaintext.\">semantic security</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"Ini adalah garis besar dasar RSA. Dalam praktiknya, [skema padding yang lebih canggih](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577) diterapkan pada teks biasa $M$ sebelum enkripsi untuk memastikan bahwa teks biasa yang sama menghasilkan ciphertext yang berbeda. Ini mencegah berbagai kemungkinan serangan terhadap implementasi RSA yang naif dan memungkinkan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Hanya dengan ciphertext, dan informasi publik apa pun yang relevan (seperti kunci publik untuk kriptografi kunci asimetris), dan penyerang tidak dapat mengambil bahkan informasi parsial dari teks biasa.\">keamanan semantis</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Illustration of RSA in Python {#illustration-of-rsa-in-python}"
msgstr "Ilustrasi RSA dalam Python {#illustration-of-rsa-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following code cells, we illustrate a simple example of the RSA "
"algorithm using small integers and then demonstrate practical key "
"distribution and digital signature applications using Python libraries "
"implementing RSA.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam sel kode berikut, kita mengilustrasikan contoh sederhana algoritma RSA"
" menggunakan bilangan bulat kecil dan kemudian mendemonstrasikan distribusi "
"kunci praktis dan aplikasi tanda tangan digital menggunakan pustaka Python "
"yang mengimplementasikan RSA.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Note: In this section we will show the math calculations in detail as part of the Python code\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Catatan: Di bagian ini kita akan menampilkan perhitungan matematika secara detail sebagai bagian dari kode Python\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "RSA key generation {#rsa-key-generation}"
msgstr "Pembuatan kunci RSA {#rsa-key-generation}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's step through a simple instance of the RSA algorithm employing small "
"prime numbers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita telusuri contoh sederhana algoritma RSA menggunakan bilangan prima"
" kecil.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will need to be able to compute the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest positive whole number "
"that can divide two or more of the given whole numbers.\">greatest common "
"divisor</DefinitionTooltip> of two integers, as it will be needed to test "
"whether two integers are <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Two numbers that "
"have a greatest common divisor of 1. For example, 3 and 13 are coprime "
"because only 1 can divide both of them.\">coprime</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita perlu bisa menghitung <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common "
"Divisor - bilangan bulat positif terbesar yang dapat membagi dua atau lebih "
"bilangan bulat yang diberikan.\">pembagi bersama "
"terbesar</DefinitionTooltip> dari dua bilangan bulat, karena itu akan "
"diperlukan untuk menguji apakah dua bilangan bulat bersifat "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Dua bilangan yang memiliki pembagi bersama "
"terbesar 1. Misalnya, 3 dan 13 adalah koprim karena hanya 1 yang dapat "
"membagi keduanya.\">koprim</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will explain one simple way to calculate this, but it is much more "
"efficient with larger integers to use the `math.gcd` python function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan menjelaskan satu cara sederhana untuk menghitung ini, tapi jauh "
"lebih efisien dengan bilangan bulat yang lebih besar untuk menggunakan "
"fungsi python `math.gcd`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first phase of the RSA workflow is key generation. This is initiated by "
"choosing two prime numbers, which are meant to be kept secret by the entity "
"generating the keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fase pertama alur kerja RSA adalah pembuatan kunci. Ini dimulai dengan "
"memilih dua bilangan prima, yang dimaksudkan untuk dijaga kerahasiaannya "
"oleh entitas yang membuat kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The modulus is the remainder left "
"over after dividing by the value specified. modulo is the operation of doing"
" this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$, which is simply the product of the"
" two chosen primes, is computed. This modulus will be published as part of "
"the public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modulus adalah sisa yang "
"tersisa setelah dibagi dengan nilai yang ditentukan. modulo adalah operasi "
"untuk melakukan ini.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$, yang merupakan hasil"
" kali dari dua prima yang dipilih, dihitung. Modulus ini akan dipublikasikan"
" sebagai bagian dari kunci publik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Euler <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The totient is a number, or "
"numbers, that are not greater than the given number, and are relatively "
"prime to it, having no factors in common.\">totient</DefinitionTooltip> "
"function <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used "
"to indicate Euler's totient.\">$\\varphi(n)$</DefinitionTooltip> is computed"
" next, as it is needed for the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an "
"integer $a$, and modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the"
" case for coprimes.\">modular multiplicative inverse</DefinitionTooltip> "
"operation used to determine the keys in RSA. $phi$ is also kept secret and "
"typically discarded after key generation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Totient adalah bilangan, atau "
"bilangan-bilangan, yang tidak lebih besar dari bilangan yang diberikan, dan "
"relatif prima terhadapnya, tidak memiliki faktor yang "
"sama.\">totient</DefinitionTooltip> Euler <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Simbol Yunani, phi, sering digunakan untuk menunjukkan totient "
"Euler.\">$\\varphi(n)$</DefinitionTooltip> dihitung berikutnya, karena "
"diperlukan untuk operasi <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Diberikan bilangan "
"bulat $a$, dan modulus $m$, sisa dari ax/m adalah 1. Ini hanya berlaku untuk"
" bilangan koprim.\">invers multiplikatif modular</DefinitionTooltip> yang "
"digunakan untuk menentukan kunci dalam RSA. $phi$ juga dijaga kerahasiaannya"
" dan biasanya dibuang setelah pembuatan kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We are now ready to calculate the public and private keys. In RSA, each of "
"these is specified by a tuple of two integers. The first entry in each tuple"
" is a distinct integer, and the second entry is the modulus $n$ that is "
"common to both keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekarang siap untuk menghitung kunci publik dan privat. Dalam RSA, "
"masing-masing ditentukan oleh tuple dua bilangan bulat. Entri pertama dalam "
"setiap tuple adalah bilangan bulat yang berbeda, dan entri kedua adalah "
"modulus $n$ yang umum untuk kedua kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first entry in the public key can be any integer greater than 1 that is "
"coprime to $phi$. Two integers are coprime if their <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest positive whole number "
"that can divide two or more of the given whole numbers.\">greatest common "
"divisor</DefinitionTooltip> is 1. So we use the `math.gcd` function find an "
"integer $e$ coprime to $phi$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Entri pertama dalam kunci publik bisa berupa bilangan bulat apa pun yang "
"lebih besar dari 1 yang koprim dengan $phi$. Dua bilangan bulat bersifat "
"koprim jika <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - "
"bilangan bulat positif terbesar yang dapat membagi dua atau lebih bilangan "
"bulat yang diberikan.\">pembagi bersama terbesar</DefinitionTooltip> mereka "
"adalah 1. Jadi kita menggunakan fungsi `math.gcd` untuk menemukan bilangan "
"bulat $e$ yang koprim dengan $phi$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The private key requires an integer $d$, which is the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Also known as reciprocal, a number, which when multiplied by "
"the number given, results in a value of 1.\">multiplicative "
"inverse</DefinitionTooltip> of $e$ modulo $phi$; that is, it satisfies the "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Consistency, or equivalence ie. all behaving"
" in the same way.\">congruency relation</DefinitionTooltip> $d*e\\equiv 1 "
"\\pmod{\\varphi(n)}$. For this simple illustration where we are dealing with"
" small integers, we can just loop over the positive integers to locate a "
"suitable $d$. In realistic settings, the computationally efficient "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An efficient way of calculating the greatest"
" common divisor of two whole numbers. It improves on the original Euclidean "
"algorithm.\">extended Euclidean algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> is used for "
"this purpose.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci privat membutuhkan bilangan bulat $d$, yang merupakan "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Juga dikenal sebagai resiprokal, sebuah "
"bilangan, yang ketika dikalikan dengan bilangan yang diberikan, menghasilkan"
" nilai 1.\">invers multiplikatif</DefinitionTooltip> dari $e$ modulo $phi$; "
"yaitu, memenuhi <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Konsistensi, atau kesetaraan"
" yaitu semua berperilaku dengan cara yang sama.\">relasi "
"kongruensi</DefinitionTooltip> $d*e\\equiv 1 \\pmod{\\varphi(n)}$. Untuk "
"ilustrasi sederhana ini di mana kita berurusan dengan bilangan bulat kecil, "
"kita cukup mengulang bilangan bulat positif untuk menemukan $d$ yang sesuai."
" Dalam pengaturan realistis, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Cara yang "
"efisien untuk menghitung pembagi bersama terbesar dari dua bilangan bulat. "
"Ini meningkatkan algoritma Euclidean asli.\">algoritma Euclidean yang "
"diperluas</DefinitionTooltip> yang efisien secara komputasi digunakan untuk "
"tujuan ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now form the tuples $(e, n), (d, n)$, which form the public and private "
"keys respectively. The public key is then published, while the private key "
"is kept secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekarang membentuk tuple $(e, n), (d, n)$, yang masing-masing membentuk"
" kunci publik dan privat. Kunci publik kemudian dipublikasikan, sementara "
"kunci privat dijaga kerahasiaannya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Encryption and decryption in RSA use the [modular exponentiation "
"operation](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Modular_exponentiation&oldid=1160764843)."
" Further, the public and private keys are complementary in that either can "
"be used to encrypt a message that the other can then decrypt.\n"
msgstr ""
"Enkripsi dan dekripsi dalam RSA menggunakan [operasi eksponensiasi "
"modular](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Modular_exponentiation&oldid=1160764843)."
" Selanjutnya, kunci publik dan privat saling melengkapi dalam hal salah satu"
" bisa digunakan untuk mengenkripsi pesan yang kemudian bisa didekripsi oleh "
"yang lain.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we illustrate the case where the public key $(e,n)$ is used for "
"encryption and the private key $(d, n)$ is used for decryption by defining a"
" Python function for each operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kita mengilustrasikan kasus di mana kunci publik $(e,n)$ digunakan "
"untuk enkripsi dan kunci privat $(d, n)$ digunakan untuk dekripsi dengan "
"mendefinisikan fungsi Python untuk setiap operasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We then encrypt and decrypt an integer message $msg$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kemudian mengenkripsi dan mendekripsi pesan bilangan bulat $msg$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the small integers used above are useful to easily outline the core "
"ideas in the RSA algorithm, in real applications RSA requires the use of "
"very large integers. For example, 2048-bit RSA involves the use of a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The modulus is the remainder left over after"
" dividing by the value specified. modulo is the operation of doing "
"this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$ that is 2048 bits long, the decimal "
"integer equivalents of which are around 10$^616$. These truly enormous "
"numbers are necessary for the practical security of RSA.\n"
msgstr ""
"Meskipun bilangan bulat kecil yang digunakan di atas berguna untuk dengan "
"mudah menguraikan ide-ide inti dalam algoritma RSA, dalam aplikasi nyata RSA"
" membutuhkan penggunaan bilangan bulat yang sangat besar. Misalnya, RSA "
"2048-bit melibatkan penggunaan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modulus "
"adalah sisa yang tersisa setelah dibagi dengan nilai yang ditentukan. modulo"
" adalah operasi untuk melakukan ini.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$ yang "
"panjangnya 2048 bit, setara dengan bilangan bulat desimal yang sekitar "
"10$^616$. Angka-angka yang sangat besar ini diperlukan untuk keamanan "
"praktis RSA.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Symmetric key exchange with RSA {#symmetric-key-exchange-with-rsa}"
msgstr ""
"Pertukaran kunci simetris dengan RSA {#symmetric-key-exchange-with-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As discussed previously, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Asynchronous key "
"encryption.\">AKC</DefinitionTooltip> enables two parties who wish to "
"communicate to securely establish a *shared secret*, which can be used, for "
"instance, as the secret key for subsequent symmetric encryption of bulk "
"plain text.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang dibahas sebelumnya, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Enkripsi "
"kunci asinkron.\">AKC</DefinitionTooltip> memungkinkan dua pihak yang ingin "
"berkomunikasi untuk menetapkan secara aman sebuah *rahasia bersama*, yang "
"bisa digunakan, misalnya, sebagai kunci rahasia untuk enkripsi simetris teks"
" biasa dalam jumlah besar berikutnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us consider the following scenario. Alice and Bob want to use "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Symmetric key "
"encryption.\">SKC</DefinitionTooltip> to encrypt and decrypt messages. "
"However, before this process can be initialized, they need to agree on a "
"common secret key. One option is for one party — say, Alice — to generate a "
"secret key and then securely transmit it to Bob. To achieve this secure "
"transfer, Alice decides to use RSA as the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Key encapsulation mechanism. Secures a symmetric key by use of "
"asymmetric key encryption. A simple approach is to encrypt a random "
"symmetric key using a public key, but more advanced & secure kems are "
"available, and new ones continually developed.\">key encapsulation "
"mechanism</DefinitionTooltip> (KEM).\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita pertimbangkan skenario berikut. Alice dan Bob ingin menggunakan "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Enkripsi kunci "
"simetris.\">SKC</DefinitionTooltip> untuk mengenkripsi dan mendekripsi "
"pesan. Namun, sebelum proses ini bisa diinisialisasi, mereka perlu "
"menyepakati kunci rahasia bersama. Salah satu opsi adalah satu pihak — "
"katakanlah, Alice — menghasilkan kunci rahasia dan kemudian mengirimkannya "
"secara aman ke Bob. Untuk mencapai transfer yang aman ini, Alice memutuskan "
"untuk menggunakan RSA sebagai <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Mekanisme "
"enkapsulasi kunci. Mengamankan kunci simetris melalui penggunaan enkripsi "
"kunci asimetris. Pendekatan sederhana adalah mengenkripsi kunci simetris "
"acak menggunakan kunci publik, tapi KEM yang lebih canggih & aman tersedia, "
"dan yang baru terus dikembangkan.\">mekanisme enkapsulasi "
"kunci</DefinitionTooltip> (KEM).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This involves the following steps:\n"
msgstr "Ini melibatkan langkah-langkah berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, Alice generates a random symmetric key, which she intends to share "
"with Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, Alice menghasilkan kunci simetris acak, yang ingin dia bagikan "
"dengan Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Bob generates an asymmetric key pair and makes his public key "
"available on a suitable channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Bob menghasilkan pasangan kunci asimetris dan membuat kunci "
"publiknya tersedia di saluran yang sesuai.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Alice uses Bob's public key to encrypt the symmetric key, thus "
"encapsulating it in a ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, Alice menggunakan kunci publik Bob untuk mengenkripsi kunci "
"simetris, sehingga mengenkapsulasi dalam sebuah ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice broadcasts the ciphertext over a reliable but not necessarily "
"secure channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Alice menyiarkan ciphertext melalui saluran yang dapat diandalkan "
"tapi tidak harus aman.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob receives the ciphertext and decrypts it using his private key. "
"He now has access to the symmetric key generated by Alice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, Bob menerima ciphertext dan mendekripsinya menggunakan kunci "
"privatnya. Dia sekarang memiliki akses ke kunci simetris yang dibuat oleh "
"Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 1. Symmetric key exchange with "
"RSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/key_exchange_rsa.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 1. Symmetric key exchange with "
"RSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/key_exchange_rsa.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 1. Symmetric key exchange with RSA*\n"
msgstr "*Gambar 1. Pertukaran kunci simetris dengan RSA*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Padding-based key-exchange example in Python {#padding-based-key-exchange-"
"example-in-python}"
msgstr ""
"Contoh pertukaran kunci berbasis padding dalam Python {#padding-based-key-"
"exchange-example-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A practical workflow utilizing RSA for padding-based non-interactive key "
"exchange is now illustrated using the ``cryptography`` Python library.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alur kerja praktis yang menggunakan RSA untuk pertukaran kunci non-"
"interaktif berbasis padding kini diilustrasikan menggunakan pustaka Python "
"``cryptography``.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Import necessary modules from the ``cryptography`` Python library. If "
"needed, this library can be installed using the command ``pip install "
"cryptography``.\n"
msgstr ""
"Impor modul yang diperlukan dari pustaka Python ``cryptography``. Jika "
"diperlukan, pustaka ini bisa diinstal menggunakan perintah ``pip install "
"cryptography``.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice then generates a random secret key, which she intends to transmit to "
"Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice kemudian menghasilkan kunci rahasia acak, yang ingin dia kirimkan ke "
"Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the ``rsa`` module from the ``cryptography`` library, Bob generates a "
"key pair and then broadcasts his public key. Any one can intercept the "
"public key and read off the public numbers $(e,n)$ that form the key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan modul ``rsa`` dari pustaka ``cryptography``, Bob menghasilkan "
"pasangan kunci lalu menyiarkan kunci publiknya. Siapa pun bisa mencegat "
"kunci publik dan membaca bilangan publik $(e,n)$ yang membentuk kunci "
"tersebut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, we assume Alice has received the public key broadcast by Bob."
" Alice's ``symmetric_key`` above can now be encrypted using Bob's public key"
" to produce the ciphertext. In a realistic setting, Alice will also use "
"additional <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The addition of data to the "
"beginning, middle, or end of a message. Often used in block ciphers to fill "
"out blocks with insufficient data up to the required "
"size.\">padding</DefinitionTooltip> methods such as "
"[OAEP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577)"
" to ensure <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"With only the ciphertext, and any"
" relevant public information (such as public key for asymmetric key "
"cryptography), and adversary cannot retrieve even partial information from "
"the plaintext.\">semantic security</DefinitionTooltip> for her "
"communications with Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada titik ini, kita asumsikan Alice telah menerima kunci publik yang "
"disiarkan oleh Bob. ``symmetric_key`` Alice di atas sekarang bisa dienkripsi"
" menggunakan kunci publik Bob untuk menghasilkan ciphertext. Dalam "
"pengaturan realistis, Alice juga akan menggunakan metode <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Penambahan data ke awal, tengah, atau akhir pesan. Sering "
"digunakan dalam block cipher untuk mengisi blok dengan data yang tidak "
"mencukupi hingga ukuran yang diperlukan.\">padding</DefinitionTooltip> "
"tambahan seperti "
"[OAEP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577)"
" untuk memastikan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Hanya dengan ciphertext, "
"dan informasi publik apa pun yang relevan (seperti kunci publik untuk "
"kriptografi kunci asimetris), dan penyerang tidak dapat mengambil bahkan "
"informasi parsial dari teks biasa.\">keamanan semantis</DefinitionTooltip> "
"untuk komunikasinya dengan Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice then broadcasts the ciphertext over an open channel, confident that "
"only Bob with the corresponding private key will be able to decrypt it. We "
"assume Bob has received the ciphertext and can now decrypt it using his "
"confidential private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice kemudian menyiarkan ciphertext melalui saluran terbuka, yakin bahwa "
"hanya Bob dengan kunci privat yang sesuai yang bisa mendekripsinya. Kita "
"asumsikan Bob telah menerima ciphertext dan sekarang bisa mendekripsinya "
"menggunakan kunci privat rahasianya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, Alice and Bob both have access to the secret symmetric key, "
"which they can use for <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Symmetric key "
"encryption.\">SKC</DefinitionTooltip> applications.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada titik ini, Alice dan Bob keduanya memiliki akses ke kunci simetris "
"rahasia, yang bisa mereka gunakan untuk aplikasi <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Enkripsi kunci simetris.\">SKC</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simulating a Key Encapsulation Mechanism with RSA in Python {#simulating-a-"
"key-encapsulation-mechanism-with-rsa-in-python}"
msgstr ""
"Mensimulasikan Mekanisme Enkapsulasi Kunci dengan RSA dalam Python "
"{#simulating-a-key-encapsulation-mechanism-with-rsa-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following workflow, we illustrate the use of RSA to simulate a Key "
"Encapsulation Mechanism (KEM) whereby a sufficiently long random secret "
"message is securely exchanged and subsequently converted into a shared-"
"secret of the appropriate length using a KDF.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam alur kerja berikut, kita mengilustrasikan penggunaan RSA untuk "
"mensimulasikan Mekanisme Enkapsulasi Kunci (KEM) di mana pesan rahasia acak "
"yang cukup panjang dipertukarkan secara aman dan kemudian dikonversi menjadi"
" rahasia bersama dengan panjang yang sesuai menggunakan KDF.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once again Alice and Bob want to establish a shared secret non-interactively"
" and Alice is the party that decides which secret to use.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekali lagi Alice dan Bob ingin menetapkan rahasia bersama secara non-"
"interaktif dan Alice adalah pihak yang menentukan rahasia mana yang "
"digunakan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We start by importing some necessary Python libraries.\n"
msgstr "Kita mulai dengan mengimpor beberapa pustaka Python yang diperlukan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob then generates his RSA key pair and broadcasts his public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bob kemudian menghasilkan pasangan kunci RSA-nya dan menyiarkan kunci "
"publiknya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice first generates a long random secret from which the shared secret will"
" be eventually derived. In a pure "
"[KEM](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_encapsulation_mechanism&oldid=1110687965),"
" the long secret will be a random element from the algebraic structure "
"underlying the cryptosystem. In the case of 2048-bit RSA, this would be a "
"random integer modulo the 2048-bit RSA modulus. As such a pure KEM does not "
"require additional padding but in this example we are only simulating a KEM "
"using RSA and the `cryptography` library requires the use of padding when "
"encrypting with RSA. So we will use a somewhat shorter long secret which "
"nevertheless is much longer than a standard 256-bit AES key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice pertama-tama menghasilkan rahasia acak yang panjang dari mana rahasia "
"bersama pada akhirnya akan diturunkan. Dalam "
"[KEM](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_encapsulation_mechanism&oldid=1110687965)"
" murni, rahasia yang panjang akan menjadi elemen acak dari struktur aljabar "
"yang mendasari kriptosistem. Dalam kasus RSA 2048-bit, ini akan menjadi "
"bilangan bulat acak modulo RSA modulus 2048-bit. Karena KEM murni seperti "
"itu tidak memerlukan padding tambahan tapi dalam contoh ini kita hanya "
"mensimulasikan KEM menggunakan RSA dan pustaka `cryptography` mengharuskan "
"penggunaan padding saat mengenkripsi dengan RSA. Jadi kita akan menggunakan "
"rahasia panjang yang agak lebih pendek yang tetap jauh lebih panjang dari "
"kunci AES 256-bit standar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next Alice encrypts the long secret using Bob's public key and the encrypted"
" secret is communicated to Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya Alice mengenkripsi rahasia panjang menggunakan kunci publik Bob "
"dan rahasia terenkripsi dikomunikasikan ke Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bob decrypt's the encrypted secret received from Alice using his private "
"key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bob mendekripsi rahasia terenkripsi yang diterima dari Alice menggunakan "
"kunci privatnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally both Alice and Bob separately apply an agreed upon [Key Derivation "
"Function](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_derivation_function&oldid=1165650237)"
" (KDF) on the long secret to derive the symmetric key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya baik Alice maupun Bob secara terpisah menerapkan [Fungsi Derivasi "
"Kunci](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_derivation_function&oldid=1165650237)"
" (KDF) yang telah disepakati pada rahasia panjang untuk menurunkan kunci "
"simetris.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that the process involves a hashing protocol and the use of a random "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Regarding password hashing, the idea that "
"salt enhances/makes a food unique is the same idea of how adding salt in "
"this context makes our password unique, distinctive, and hard to "
"reproduce.\">*salt*</DefinitionTooltip> which ensures uniqueness and "
"unpredictability of the shared symmetric key in case the long secret is ever"
" reused (not recommended). However the *salt* itself does not have to be "
"secret and once it is randomly generated, say by Alice in this example, it "
"can be broadcasted to Bob alongside the encrypted long secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa prosesnya melibatkan protokol hashing dan penggunaan "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Mengenai hashing kata sandi, ide bahwa garam"
" meningkatkan/membuat makanan menjadi unik adalah ide yang sama tentang "
"bagaimana menambahkan garam dalam konteks ini membuat kata sandi kita unik, "
"khas, dan sulit direproduksi.\">*salt*</DefinitionTooltip> acak yang "
"memastikan keunikan dan ketidakpastian kunci simetris bersama jika rahasia "
"panjang pernah digunakan kembali (tidak disarankan). Namun *salt* itu "
"sendiri tidak harus rahasia dan setelah dibuat secara acak, katakanlah oleh "
"Alice dalam contoh ini, bisa disiarkan ke Bob bersama rahasia panjang yang "
"terenkripsi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will assume therefore that both Alice and Bob have access to the same "
"random *salt*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan mengasumsikan bahwa baik Alice maupun Bob memiliki akses ke *salt*"
" acak yang sama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Digital signatures with RSA {#digital-signatures-with-rsa}"
msgstr "Tanda tangan digital dengan RSA {#digital-signatures-with-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will now extend the above confidential communication scenario with Alice "
"and Bob to one that also includes validation with the help of a [digital "
"signature](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191).\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekarang akan memperluas skenario komunikasi rahasia di atas antara "
"Alice dan Bob ke skenario yang juga menyertakan validasi dengan bantuan "
"[tanda tangan "
"digital](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As before, Alice will confidentially send a message encapsulating a "
"symmetric key to Bob, but she will also digitally sign the message so that "
"Bob, upon receiving the message, can verify that it was Alice who originated"
" it and that the contents of the message were not tampered with during "
"transmission.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti sebelumnya, Alice akan secara rahasia mengirim pesan yang "
"mengenkapsulasi kunci simetris ke Bob, tapi dia juga akan menandatangani "
"pesan secara digital sehingga Bob, setelah menerima pesan, bisa "
"memverifikasi bahwa itu Alice yang berasal darinya dan bahwa isi pesan tidak"
" dirusak selama transmisi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"More generally, it is desirable to enable validation without compromising "
"confidentiality whereby any interested party is able to verify the "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Integrity is maintained when a message is "
"protected against unauthorized change.\">integrity</DefinitionTooltip>, "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is "
"from the source it claims to be from.\">authenticity</DefinitionTooltip>, "
"and establish non-repudiation with respect to a given communication, even if"
" that party does not have access to the actual plain text message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara lebih umum, diinginkan untuk memungkinkan validasi tanpa mengorbankan"
" kerahasiaan di mana pihak mana pun bisa memverifikasi <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Integritas dipertahankan ketika pesan dilindungi dari perubahan"
" yang tidak sah.\">integritas</DefinitionTooltip>, <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Keaslian adalah bukti bahwa pesan berasal dari sumber yang "
"diklaim.\">keaslian</DefinitionTooltip>, dan menetapkan non-repudiation "
"terkait komunikasi tertentu, bahkan jika pihak tersebut tidak memiliki akses"
" ke pesan teks biasa yang sebenarnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will consider this general setting which then involves the following "
"steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan mempertimbangkan pengaturan umum ini yang kemudian melibatkan "
"langkah-langkah berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, both Bob and Alice make their public keys available over an open "
"channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, baik Bob maupun Alice membuat kunci publik mereka tersedia melalui "
"saluran terbuka.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice encrypts the plain text using Bob's public key, creating a "
"ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Alice mengenkripsi teks biasa menggunakan kunci publik Bob, "
"membuat ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Alice creates a hash of the ciphertext with a *hash function* and "
"further encrypts the resulting hashed ciphertext using her private key. This"
" encrypted hash is the *signature*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, Alice membuat hash dari ciphertext dengan sebuah *fungsi hash* "
"dan lebih lanjut mengenkripsi ciphertext yang di-hash menggunakan kunci "
"privatnya. Hash terenkripsi ini adalah *tanda tangan*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice then transmits both the ciphertext and the signature over an "
"open channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Alice kemudian mengirimkan ciphertext dan tanda tangan melalui "
"saluran terbuka.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Bob uses Alice's public key to decrypt the signature, revealing the "
"hashed ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Bob menggunakan kunci publik Alice untuk mendekripsi tanda tangan,"
" mengungkapkan ciphertext yang di-hash.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, since Bob also has access to the ciphertext itself, he uses the same "
"hash function used by Alice to recreate a second instance of the hashed "
"ciphertext. If the latter matches the one obtained by decrypting Alice's "
"signature, then the message is validated, even though the ciphertext itself "
"has not yet been decrypted.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, karena Bob juga memiliki akses ke ciphertext itu sendiri, dia "
"menggunakan fungsi hash yang sama yang digunakan Alice untuk membuat "
"instance kedua dari ciphertext yang di-hash. Jika yang terakhir cocok dengan"
" yang diperoleh dengan mendekripsi tanda tangan Alice, maka pesan telah "
"divalidasi, meskipun ciphertext itu sendiri belum didekripsi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob, having validated the message, decrypts the ciphertext using "
"his own private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, Bob, setelah memvalidasi pesan, mendekripsi ciphertext menggunakan"
" kunci privatnya sendiri.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 2. Digital signatures with RSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/dig_sig_rsa.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 2. Digital signatures with RSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/dig_sig_rsa.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 2. Digital signatures with RSA*\n"
msgstr "*Gambar 2. Tanda tangan digital dengan RSA*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This workflow for a digital signature is illustrated next.\n"
msgstr "Alur kerja untuk tanda tangan digital ini diilustrasikan berikutnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We once again import some useful modules from the ``cryptography`` library.\n"
"As before, Alice intends to securely send a symmetric key to Bob, but she also wishes to digitally sign it. In this case, we need public keys for both Alice and Bob. Therefore, the first step is for both Alice and Bob to create their own key pair using RSA and broadcast their own public key to the world.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekali lagi mengimpor beberapa modul berguna dari pustaka ``cryptography``.\n"
"Seperti sebelumnya, Alice bermaksud untuk secara aman mengirim kunci simetris ke Bob, tapi dia juga ingin menandatanganinya secara digital. Dalam hal ini, kita membutuhkan kunci publik untuk baik Alice maupun Bob. Oleh karena itu, langkah pertama adalah baik Alice maupun Bob membuat pasangan kunci mereka sendiri menggunakan RSA dan menyiarkan kunci publik mereka sendiri ke dunia.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next step, as before, Alice uses Bob's public key to encrypt the "
"symmetric key and prepares the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada langkah berikutnya, seperti sebelumnya, Alice menggunakan kunci publik "
"Bob untuk mengenkripsi kunci simetris dan menyiapkan ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this stage, instead of just broadcasting the ciphertext, Alice intends to"
" attach a digital signature to it so that she can prove to Bob that she was "
"the sender of the message. This is done in two steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada tahap ini, alih-alih hanya menyiarkan ciphertext, Alice bermaksud untuk"
" melampirkan tanda tangan digital ke dalamnya sehingga dia bisa membuktikan "
"kepada Bob bahwa dia adalah pengirim pesan. Ini dilakukan dalam dua "
"langkah:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create a hash of the ciphertext using a hashing algorithm.\n"
msgstr "Buat hash dari ciphertext menggunakan algoritma hashing.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Encrypt the hash using Alice's private key, which amounts to a signature.\n"
msgstr ""
"Enkripsi hash menggunakan kunci privat Alice, yang merupakan sebuah tanda "
"tangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice then broadcasts the ciphertext and the signature over a network so "
"that Bob is able to intercept both of them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice kemudian menyiarkan ciphertext dan tanda tangan melalui jaringan "
"sehingga Bob bisa mencegat keduanya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On Bob's side, the first task is to verify the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Integrity is maintained when a message is protected against "
"unauthorized change.\">integrity</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is from the source it "
"claims to be from.\">authenticity</DefinitionTooltip> of the ciphertext. To "
"do this, Bob creates a hash of the received ciphertext using the same "
"hashing algorithm used by Alice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sisi Bob, tugas pertama adalah memverifikasi <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Integritas dipertahankan ketika pesan dilindungi dari perubahan"
" yang tidak sah.\">integritas</DefinitionTooltip> dan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Keaslian adalah bukti bahwa pesan berasal dari sumber yang "
"diklaim.\">keaslian</DefinitionTooltip> ciphertext. Untuk melakukan ini, Bob"
" membuat hash dari ciphertext yang diterima menggunakan algoritma hashing "
"yang sama yang digunakan Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Bob decrypts the received signature using Alice's public key. Because "
"Alice used her private key to create the signature, Bob is able to decrypt "
"it using Alice's public key. The decrypted signature is nothing but a hash "
"of the ciphertext created on Alice's end. If the hash created by Bob matches"
" the decrypted signature, then Bob has verified that the ciphertext he "
"received has not been tampered with and that it was Alice who signed the "
"ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Bob mendekripsi tanda tangan yang diterima menggunakan kunci "
"publik Alice. Karena Alice menggunakan kunci privatnya untuk membuat tanda "
"tangan, Bob bisa mendekripsinya menggunakan kunci publik Alice. Tanda tangan"
" yang didekripsi tidak lain adalah hash dari ciphertext yang dibuat di sisi "
"Alice. Jika hash yang dibuat oleh Bob cocok dengan tanda tangan yang "
"didekripsi, maka Bob telah memverifikasi bahwa ciphertext yang dia terima "
"tidak dirusak dan bahwa itu Alice yang menandatangani ciphertext tersebut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the Python code below, these operations are combined into a useful "
"utility function called ``verify`` provided by an object associated with "
"Alice's public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kode Python di bawah ini, operasi-operasi ini digabungkan ke dalam "
"fungsi utilitas berguna yang disebut ``verify`` yang disediakan oleh objek "
"yang terkait dengan kunci publik Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Having verified the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Integrity is maintained "
"when a message is protected against unauthorized "
"change.\">integrity</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is from the source it "
"claims to be from.\">authenticity</DefinitionTooltip> of the received "
"ciphertext, Bob can then decrypt it using his private key because Alice "
"created the ciphertext using Bob's public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah memverifikasi <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Integritas "
"dipertahankan ketika pesan dilindungi dari perubahan yang tidak "
"sah.\">integritas</DefinitionTooltip> dan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Keaslian adalah bukti bahwa pesan berasal dari sumber yang "
"diklaim.\">keaslian</DefinitionTooltip> ciphertext yang diterima, Bob "
"kemudian bisa mendekripsinya menggunakan kunci privatnya karena Alice "
"membuat ciphertext menggunakan kunci publik Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above digital signature scenario, any party — not just Bob — can "
"verify that Alice is the sender of the ciphertext because everyone can "
"access Alice's public key, the ciphertext, and the digital signature. "
"Furthermore, after sending the ciphertext and the signature, Alice cannot "
"later deny having done so because the signature can be decrypted to a "
"meaningful hash using only her public key. This establishes "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Non-repudiation refers to the ability to "
"prove that a specific party has sent a message. In symmetric key "
"cryptography, since the same key is used for both encryption and decryption,"
" it is not possible to determine which party has created a particular "
"ciphertext. In contrast, asymmetric key cryptography provides non-"
"repudiation through the use of digital signatures.\">non-"
"repudiation</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam skenario tanda tangan digital di atas, pihak mana pun — bukan hanya "
"Bob — bisa memverifikasi bahwa Alice adalah pengirim ciphertext karena semua"
" orang bisa mengakses kunci publik Alice, ciphertext, dan tanda tangan "
"digital. Selanjutnya, setelah mengirim ciphertext dan tanda tangan, Alice "
"tidak bisa kemudian menyangkal telah melakukannya karena tanda tangan bisa "
"didekripsi menjadi hash yang bermakna hanya menggunakan kunci publiknya. Ini"
" menetapkan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Non-repudiation mengacu pada "
"kemampuan untuk membuktikan bahwa pihak tertentu telah mengirim pesan. Dalam"
" kriptografi kunci simetris, karena kunci yang sama digunakan untuk enkripsi"
" dan dekripsi, tidak mungkin menentukan pihak mana yang membuat ciphertext "
"tertentu. Sebaliknya, kriptografi kunci asimetris menyediakan non-"
"repudiation melalui penggunaan tanda tangan digital.\">non-"
"repudiation</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By enabling secure key distribution and supporting non-repudiation, public "
"key cryptography establishes a strong foundation for secure digital "
"communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan memungkinkan distribusi kunci yang aman dan mendukung non-"
"repudiation, kriptografi kunci publik menetapkan fondasi yang kuat untuk "
"komunikasi digital yang aman.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Breaking RSA {#breaking-rsa}"
msgstr "Membobol RSA {#breaking-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The utility and security of the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-key"
" cryptosystem named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. "
"Developed in 1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip> algorithm outlined above rests "
"on two mathematical assumptions:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kegunaan dan keamanan algoritma <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-key"
" cryptosystem named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. "
"Developed in 1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip> yang diuraikan di atas bertumpu"
" pada dua asumsi matematis:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finding the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, and "
"modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">modular multiplicative inverse</DefinitionTooltip> $d$ given "
"that access only to $(e, n)$ is computationally infeasible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mencari <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, and modulus "
"$m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">invers perkalian modular</DefinitionTooltip> $d$ dengan hanya "
"memiliki akses ke $(e, n)$ secara komputasi tidak layak dilakukan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the RSA setting, the modular exponentiation operation behaves like a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A one-way function where it is easy to "
"compute an output from the inputs, but hard to determine the inputs from the"
" output.\">one-way trapdoor function</DefinitionTooltip>. When used for "
"encryption, it yields ciphertext that is inscrutable, and without access to "
"the private key, inverting the operation to recover the plain text from the "
"ciphertext is not feasible. However, with access to the private key, which "
"acts as a trapdoor, the ciphertext can be easily decrypted.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam konteks RSA, operasi eksponen modular berperilaku seperti "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A one-way function where it is easy to "
"compute an output from the inputs, but hard to determine the inputs from the"
" output.\">fungsi trapdoor satu arah</DefinitionTooltip>. Ketika digunakan "
"untuk enkripsi, fungsi ini menghasilkan ciphertext yang tidak terbaca, dan "
"tanpa akses ke kunci privat, membalikkan operasi untuk memulihkan teks biasa"
" dari ciphertext tidaklah layak. Namun, dengan akses ke kunci privat yang "
"bertindak sebagai trapdoor, ciphertext dapat dengan mudah didekripsi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The most prominent attack on the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-"
"key cryptosystem named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. "
"Developed in 1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip> algorithm aims to undermine "
"assumption 1 by efficiently recovering the private key number $d$ via "
"factorizing the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The modulus is the remainder"
" left over after dividing by the value specified. modulo is the operation of"
" doing this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$. As will be illustrated "
"below, it is easy to recover $d$ if one has access to either the "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"prime factors of a number n, are those "
"primes that are multiplied together to make n.\">prime "
"factors</DefinitionTooltip> $p$ and $q$ of $n$ or the totient "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to "
"indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$. Recall that $p$, "
"$q$, and <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used "
"to indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ are kept secret "
"during key generation and discarded after. A third party that recovers this "
"information using a classical or quantum computer essentially uncovers the "
"private key, breaking RSA. Thus, prime factorization is the key "
"computational primitive necessary for breaking RSA.\n"
msgstr ""
"Serangan paling menonjol terhadap algoritma <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A public-key cryptosystem named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, "
"and Leonard Adleman. Developed in 1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip> bertujuan "
"merusak asumsi 1 dengan cara memulihkan nomor kunci privat $d$ secara "
"efisien melalui pemfaktoran <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The modulus is "
"the remainder left over after dividing by the value specified. modulo is the"
" operation of doing this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$. Seperti yang "
"akan diilustrasikan di bawah, mudah untuk memulihkan $d$ jika seseorang "
"memiliki akses ke <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"prime factors of a number "
"n, are those primes that are multiplied together to make n.\">faktor "
"prima</DefinitionTooltip> $p$ dan $q$ dari $n$ atau totient "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to "
"indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$. Ingatlah bahwa "
"$p$, $q$, dan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often "
"used to indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ disimpan "
"sebagai rahasia selama pembuatan kunci dan dibuang setelahnya. Pihak ketiga "
"yang memulihkan informasi ini menggunakan komputer klasik atau kuantum pada "
"dasarnya mengungkap kunci privat, sehingga membobol RSA. Oleh karena itu, "
"faktorisasi prima adalah primitif komputasi kunci yang diperlukan untuk "
"membobol RSA.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical computing and RSA {#classical-computing-and-rsa}"
msgstr "Komputasi klasik dan RSA {#classical-computing-and-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prime factorization of large integers is known to exhibit <DefinitionTooltip"
" definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial; for example, an exponential "
"function.\">super-polynomial</DefinitionTooltip> or <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Scaling slower than exponential. For example polynomial and "
"linear scaling.\">subexponential</DefinitionTooltip> scaling on classical "
"computers. The best-known classical algorithm for factoring integers larger "
"than $10^{100}$ is the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"General Number Field "
"Sieve - An efficient classical algorithm for factoring large "
"integers.\">*general number field sieve*</DefinitionTooltip> "
"[(GNFS)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=General_number_field_sieve&oldid=1151781536)\n"
msgstr ""
"Faktorisasi prima dari bilangan bulat besar diketahui memiliki skalabilitas "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial; for "
"example, an exponential function.\">super-polinomial</DefinitionTooltip> "
"atau <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Scaling slower than exponential. For "
"example polynomial and linear scaling.\">subeksponensial</DefinitionTooltip>"
" pada komputer klasik. Algoritma klasik terbaik yang diketahui untuk "
"memfaktorkan bilangan bulat lebih besar dari $10^{100}$ adalah "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"General Number Field Sieve - An efficient "
"classical algorithm for factoring large integers.\">*general number field "
"sieve*</DefinitionTooltip> "
"[(GNFS)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=General_number_field_sieve&oldid=1151781536)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$L_n[\\frac{1}{3}, (\\frac{64}{9})^{(\\frac{1}{3})}] = "
"e^{[((\\frac{64}{9})^{(\\frac{1}{3})} + o(1)) "
"(log(n))^{\\frac{1}{3}}(log(log(n))^{\\frac{2}{3}})]}$\n"
msgstr ""
"$L_n[\\frac{1}{3}, (\\frac{64}{9})^{(\\frac{1}{3})}] = "
"e^{[((\\frac{64}{9})^{(\\frac{1}{3})} + o(1)) "
"(log(n))^{\\frac{1}{3}}(log(log(n))^{\\frac{2}{3}})]}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "as a function of the integer $n$ to be factorized.\n"
msgstr "sebagai fungsi dari bilangan bulat $n$ yang akan difaktorkan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This scaling is super-polynomial in the number of bits required to represent"
" $n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Skalabilitas ini bersifat super-polinomial dalam jumlah bit yang diperlukan "
"untuk merepresentasikan $n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, prime factorization is considered inefficient on classical "
"computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh karena itu, faktorisasi prima dianggap tidak efisien pada komputer "
"klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At present, the [largest integers factored on classical "
"hardware](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_Factoring_Challenge&oldid=1163481797)"
" are in the range of 829 bits or 250 decimal digits. Given the exponential "
"growth in classical computing power that has been witnessed over the last "
"several decades, 1024-bit RSA is no longer considered secure in the near "
"term and is now deprecated. Nevertheless, in the foreseeable future, "
"factoring 2048-bit integers whose magnitude are in the range of $10^{617}$ "
"is at present considered infeasible on classical systems, suggesting "
"continued viability. The advent of quantum computers, however, voids this "
"assessment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Saat ini, [bilangan bulat terbesar yang difaktorkan pada perangkat keras "
"klasik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_Factoring_Challenge&oldid=1163481797)"
" berada dalam kisaran 829 bit atau 250 digit desimal. Mengingat pertumbuhan "
"eksponensial dalam daya komputasi klasik yang telah diamati selama beberapa "
"dekade terakhir, RSA 1024-bit tidak lagi dianggap aman dalam waktu dekat dan"
" kini sudah tidak digunakan. Meskipun demikian, di masa mendatang yang dapat"
" terlihat, memfaktorkan bilangan bulat 2048-bit yang besarnya berada dalam "
"kisaran $10^{617}$ saat ini dianggap tidak layak pada sistem klasik, yang "
"mengisyaratkan kelanjutan kegunaannya. Namun, hadirnya komputer kuantum "
"membatalkan penilaian ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shor's quantum algorithm and RSA {#shors-quantum-algorithm-and-rsa}"
msgstr "Algoritma kuantum Shor dan RSA {#shors-quantum-algorithm-and-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Probably the most well-known quantum algorithm today is <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A quantum algorithm which can find prime factors efficiently. "
"Developed by the mathematician, Peter Shor, in 1994.\">Shor's "
"algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> for finding the prime factors of integers. "
"When [introduced by Peter Shor in "
"1994](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700), it was recognized as the "
"first quantum algorithm that offered a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial; for example, an exponential "
"function.\">super-polynomial speedup</DefinitionTooltip> relative to "
"classical algorithms on a problem of great practical importance, namely "
"prime factorization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma kuantum yang mungkin paling terkenal saat ini adalah "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum algorithm which can find prime "
"factors efficiently. Developed by the mathematician, Peter Shor, in "
"1994.\">algoritma Shor</DefinitionTooltip> untuk menemukan faktor prima dari"
" bilangan bulat. Ketika [diperkenalkan oleh Peter Shor pada tahun "
"1994](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700), algoritma ini diakui "
"sebagai algoritma kuantum pertama yang menawarkan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial; for example, an exponential "
"function.\">percepatan super-polinomial</DefinitionTooltip> relatif terhadap"
" algoritma klasik pada masalah yang sangat penting secara praktis, yaitu "
"faktorisasi prima.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: Algoritma Shor
# dapat memfaktorkan prima dengan $O(n^2)$ di m
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor's algorithm can factor primes with $O(n^2)$ where $n$ is the number of bits.\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical explanation of Shor's algorithm\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: <Accordion>
# <AccordionItem title="Penjelasan matematis algor
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the context of <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-key cryptosystem "
"named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. Developed in "
"1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip>, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum "
"algorithm which can find prime factors efficiently. Developed by the "
"mathematician, Peter Shor, in 1994.\">Shor's algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> "
"works by exploiting the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at "
"which a function repeats itself.\">periodicity</DefinitionTooltip> of the "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modular exponentiation is the remainder when"
" an integer is raised to a power (exponent) and then divided by a number "
"(modulus). For example $x^e mod m$.\">modular exponential "
"function</DefinitionTooltip> $f(x) = a^x (mod~n)$ and provides a quantum "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip>-finding primitive that enables "
"efficient prime factorization of the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"modulus is the remainder left over after dividing by the value specified. "
"modulo is the operation of doing this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: Dalam konteks
# <DefinitionTooltip definition="A public-key cr
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A simplified high-level outline of Shor's overall scheme for breaking RSA is"
" as follows:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the modulus $n$, which is published as part of the public key, choose "
"a number $a$ coprime to $n$ that is, $gcd(a,n) = 1$. Since we know that $n ="
" p*q$ has exactly two prime factors $(p, q)$, almost any number less than "
"$n$ that we pick at random is likely to be coprime to $n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan modulus $n$, yang dipublikasikan sebagai bagian dari kunci publik,"
" pilih sebuah angka $a$ yang koprima terhadap $n$, yaitu, $gcd(a,n) = 1$. "
"Karena kita tahu bahwa $n = p*q$ memiliki tepat dua faktor prima $(p, q)$, "
"hampir semua angka lebih kecil dari $n$ yang kita pilih secara acak "
"kemungkinan besar akan koprima terhadap $n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Having chosen $a$, find the exponent $r$ such that $a^r \\equiv 1 (mod~n)$. "
"This implies $a^r - 1 \\equiv 0 (mod~n)$. The existence of an "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The number of times a number is multiplied "
"by itself.\">exponent</DefinitionTooltip> $r$ such that the above "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Consistency, or equivalence ie. all behaving"
" in the same way.\">congruence</DefinitionTooltip> holds is guaranteed by "
"the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats"
" itself.\">periodicity property</DefinitionTooltip> of <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Modular exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is "
"raised to a power (exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For "
"example $x^e mod m$.\">modular exponentiation</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah memilih $a$, temukan eksponen $r$ sehingga $a^r \\equiv 1 (mod~n)$. "
"Ini berarti $a^r - 1 \\equiv 0 (mod~n)$. Keberadaan sebuah "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The number of times a number is multiplied "
"by itself.\">eksponen</DefinitionTooltip> $r$ sehingga <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Consistency, or equivalence ie. all behaving in the same "
"way.\">kongruensi</DefinitionTooltip> di atas terpenuhi dijamin oleh "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">sifat periodisitas</DefinitionTooltip> dari <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Modular exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is "
"raised to a power (exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For "
"example $x^e mod m$.\">eksponen modular</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $r$ is even, $a^r - 1 \\equiv 0 (mod~n) \\implies (a^{r/2} - 1) (a^{r/2} "
"+ 1) =  \\gamma*n$ for some integer $\\gamma$. The left-hand side of this "
"latter equality must contain $p$ and $q$ as two of its prime factors since "
"the right-hand side does. If $r$ is odd, go back to step 1 and try a "
"different choice for $a$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $r$ genap, $a^r - 1 \\equiv 0 (mod~n) \\implies (a^{r/2} - 1) (a^{r/2} "
"+ 1) =  \\gamma*n$ untuk suatu bilangan bulat $\\gamma$. Sisi kiri dari "
"kesamaan tersebut harus mengandung $p$ dan $q$ sebagai dua faktor primanya "
"karena sisi kanan juga demikian. Jika $r$ ganjil, kembali ke langkah 1 dan "
"coba pilihan yang berbeda untuk $a$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An efficient way of calculating the "
"greatest common divisor of two whole numbers. It improves on the original "
"Euclidean algorithm.\">extended Euclid algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> for "
"finding $gcd((a^{r/2} - 1), n)$ or $gcd((a^{r/2} + 1), n)$. The computed "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest "
"positive whole number that can divide two or more of the given whole "
"numbers.\">GCD</DefinitionTooltip>is very likely to identify one of the "
"prime factors $p$ or $q$. Divide $n$ with this prime factor to recover the "
"other.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An efficient way of calculating the "
"greatest common divisor of two whole numbers. It improves on the original "
"Euclidean algorithm.\">algoritma Euclid yang diperluas</DefinitionTooltip> "
"untuk mencari $gcd((a^{r/2} - 1), n)$ atau $gcd((a^{r/2} + 1), n)$. "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest "
"positive whole number that can divide two or more of the given whole "
"numbers.\">GCD</DefinitionTooltip> yang dihitung kemungkinan besar akan "
"mengidentifikasi salah satu faktor prima $p$ atau $q$. Bagi $n$ dengan "
"faktor prima ini untuk memulihkan yang lainnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once $p, q$ are known, use the steps from the original RSA algorithm for "
"reconstructing the totient $\\phi(n)$ and generating the private key number "
"$d$ as the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, and modulus"
" $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">modular inverse</DefinitionTooltip> of the known public key "
"number $e$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah $p, q$ diketahui, gunakan langkah-langkah dari algoritma RSA asli "
"untuk merekonstruksi totient $\\phi(n)$ dan menghasilkan nomor kunci privat "
"$d$ sebagai <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, and "
"modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">invers modular</DefinitionTooltip> dari nomor kunci publik $e$ "
"yang diketahui.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: Pada Agustus
# 2023, Oded Regev [mempublikasikan peningkatan](
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"In August 2023 Oded Regev [published an improvement](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2308.06572) on Shor's original using a multi-dimensional approach resulting in $O(n^{1.5})$. There continues to be further research including by [Ragavan and Vaikuntanathan](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2310.00899) in this area which may improve time, cost, or number of qubits needed. Whilst we cannot say when running such algorithms against real-world RSA encryption truly becomes viable, it is becoming closer all the time.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Python example demonstrating breaking RSA encryption {#python-example-"
"demonstrating-breaking-rsa-encryption}"
msgstr ""
"Contoh Python yang mendemonstrasikan pembobol enkripsi RSA {#python-example-"
"demonstrating-breaking-rsa-encryption}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following code cells, we illustrate an example of finding a private "
"key given only the public key. This will use brute-force classical "
"computation, but shows how Shor's algorithm could be used - including large "
"keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam sel kode berikut, kita mengilustrasikan contoh pencarian kunci privat "
"hanya dengan diberikan kunci publik. Ini akan menggunakan komputasi klasik "
"dengan brute-force, tetapi menunjukkan bagaimana algoritma Shor bisa "
"digunakan — termasuk untuk kunci yang besar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"In this section we will show the math calculations in detail as part of the Python code\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Di bagian ini kita akan menampilkan kalkulasi matematis secara detail sebagai bagian dari kode Python\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the example, we have a public key $(5, 247)$, and we will recover the "
"private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini, kita memiliki kunci publik $(5, 247)$, dan kita akan "
"memulihkan kunci privat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 1:** The first step is to pick a number coprime to 247. Almost any "
"number we guess will do the job. Let's pick 6.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 1:** Langkah pertama adalah memilih angka yang koprima terhadap "
"247. Hampir semua angka yang kita tebak akan cocok. Mari pilih 6.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 2:** Next we need to find the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"interval at which a function repeats itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip> "
"$r$ such that $6^r \\equiv 1 (mod~247)$. In this example, we compute $r$ "
"classically using brute force, but we could also use Shor's algorithm on a "
"quantum computer using <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An open-source SDK "
"for working with quantum algorithms and computers. Developed by "
"IBM.\">Qiskit</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 2:** Selanjutnya kita perlu menemukan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">periode</DefinitionTooltip> $r$ sehingga $6^r \\equiv 1 "
"(mod~247)$. Dalam contoh ini, kita menghitung $r$ secara klasik menggunakan "
"brute force, tetapi kita juga bisa menggunakan algoritma Shor pada komputer "
"kuantum menggunakan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An open-source SDK for "
"working with quantum algorithms and computers. Developed by "
"IBM.\">Qiskit</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 3:** Since the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which "
"a function repeats itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip> $r = 36$ is even, we"
" can compute $f1 = (a^{r/2}-1), f2=(a^{r/2}+1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 3:** Karena <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which "
"a function repeats itself.\">periode</DefinitionTooltip> $r = 36$ adalah "
"genap, kita dapat menghitung $f1 = (a^{r/2}-1), f2=(a^{r/2}+1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 4:** Find the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor"
" - the largest positive whole number that can divide two or more of the "
"given whole numbers.\">GCD</DefinitionTooltip> of either of those factors "
"with $n$. Simply divide $n$ with the prime factor already found to obtain "
"the second prime factor.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 4:** Temukan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common "
"Divisor - the largest positive whole number that can divide two or more of "
"the given whole numbers.\">GCD</DefinitionTooltip> dari salah satu faktor "
"tersebut dengan $n$. Cukup bagi $n$ dengan faktor prima yang sudah ditemukan"
" untuk mendapatkan faktor prima kedua.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 5:** Having recovered the prime factors of $n = 247$ as "
"$p_{found}=13$ and $q_{found}=19$, we compute the totient $\\phi_{found} = "
"(p_{found}-1)*(q_{found}-1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 5:** Setelah memulihkan faktor prima dari $n = 247$ sebagai "
"$p_{found}=13$ dan $q_{found}=19$, kita menghitung totient $\\phi_{found} = "
"(p_{found}-1)*(q_{found}-1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The private key is the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$,"
" and modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">modular inverse</DefinitionTooltip> of the public key number "
"$e=5$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci privat adalah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, "
"and modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">invers modular</DefinitionTooltip> dari nomor kunci publik "
"$e=5$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above scheme, step 2 is the crucial <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip>-finding operation for which [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Shor%27s_algorithm&oldid=1164409434)"
" uses two fundamental quantum primitives, namely the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A quantum algorithm that can be used to find periodic patterns."
" Named after the fourier transform in classical physics which can split a "
"signal into a set of sine waves.\">*quantum Fourier "
"transform*</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum"
" algorithm used to estimate phase in qubits, named after phase estimation in"
" classical physics.\">*quantum phase estimation*</DefinitionTooltip>. For a "
"detailed explanation of the quantum aspects of Shor's algorithm, see the "
"Phase estimation and factoring lesson in the [Fundamentals of Quantum "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms). Steps 1 "
"and 3 through 5 involve relatively inexpensive operations that can be easily"
" carried out on classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam skema di atas, langkah 2 adalah operasi pencarian <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">periode</DefinitionTooltip> yang krusial, di mana [algoritma "
"Shor](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Shor%27s_algorithm&oldid=1164409434)"
" menggunakan dua primitif kuantum fundamental, yaitu <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A quantum algorithm that can be used to find periodic patterns."
" Named after the fourier transform in classical physics which can split a "
"signal into a set of sine waves.\">*transformasi Fourier "
"kuantum*</DefinitionTooltip> dan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum "
"algorithm used to estimate phase in qubits, named after phase estimation in "
"classical physics.\">*estimasi fase kuantum*</DefinitionTooltip>. Untuk "
"penjelasan terperinci tentang aspek kuantum dari algoritma Shor, lihat "
"pelajaran Estimasi fase dan pemfaktoran dalam [Fundamentals of Quantum "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms). Langkah 1"
" dan 3 hingga 5 melibatkan operasi yang relatif murah dan dapat dengan mudah"
" dilakukan pada komputer klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optionally, here's a detailed visual walkthrough of implementing [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EdJ7RoWcU48&t=325s).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai opsional, berikut adalah panduan visual terperinci untuk "
"mengimplementasikan [algoritma "
"Shor](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EdJ7RoWcU48&t=325s).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On quantum computers, Shor's algorithm can exhibit <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"An algorithm which scales similar to logarithmic scaling, that "
"is, efficiently compared to the size of data. A binary search is a simple "
"example.\">polylogarithmic scaling</DefinitionTooltip> as favorable as "
"$O((log~n)^2 (log~log~n))$ in terms of the modulus $n$, or "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Scales relative to a power, for example n^3."
" Grows quicker than linear scaling, but slower than "
"exponential.\">polynomial scaling</DefinitionTooltip> in terms of the number"
" of bits needed to represent $n$. This is a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial, for example an exponential "
"function.\">super-polynomial speedup</DefinitionTooltip> compared to the "
"classical <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"General Number Field Sieve - An "
"efficient classical algorithm for factoring large integers.\">GNFS "
"algorithm</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada komputer kuantum, algoritma Shor dapat menunjukkan skalabilitas "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An algorithm which scales similar to "
"logarithmic scaling, that is, efficiently compared to the size of data. A "
"binary search is a simple example.\">polilogatritmik</DefinitionTooltip> "
"sebaik $O((log~n)^2 (log~log~n))$ dalam hal modulus $n$, atau skalabilitas "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Scales relative to a power, for example n^3."
" Grows quicker than linear scaling, but slower than "
"exponential.\">polinomial</DefinitionTooltip> dalam hal jumlah bit yang "
"diperlukan untuk merepresentasikan $n$. Ini adalah <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial, for example an exponential "
"function.\">percepatan super-polinomial</DefinitionTooltip> dibandingkan "
"dengan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"General Number Field Sieve - An "
"efficient classical algorithm for factoring large integers.\">algoritma GNFS"
" klasik</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Recent resource estimates](https://quantum-"
"journal.org/papers/q-2021-04-15-433/) indicate that based on certain "
"assumptions made regarding the hardware configuration, a few tens of "
"thousands to several million <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum bit, "
"the equivalent of a bit in classical computing. A qubit behaves very "
"differently since it can be in superposition, (imagine a combination of "
"states), but once measured the superposition collapses, and the result will "
"be 0 or 1.\">qubits</DefinitionTooltip> will be necessary to break 2048-bit "
"RSA using Shor's algorithm. It is not inconceivable that quantum computers "
"with several tens of thousands of qubits will become available over the next"
" several years, making the lower end of the resource estimate accessible.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Estimasi sumber daya terbaru](https://quantum-"
"journal.org/papers/q-2021-04-15-433/) menunjukkan bahwa berdasarkan asumsi "
"tertentu mengenai konfigurasi perangkat keras, beberapa puluhan ribu hingga "
"beberapa juta <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum bit, the equivalent "
"of a bit in classical computing. A qubit behaves very differently since it "
"can be in superposition, (imagine a combination of states), but once "
"measured the superposition collapses, and the result will be 0 or "
"1.\">qubit</DefinitionTooltip> akan diperlukan untuk membobol RSA 2048-bit "
"menggunakan algoritma Shor. Tidak mustahil bahwa komputer kuantum dengan "
"beberapa puluhan ribu qubit akan tersedia dalam beberapa tahun ke depan, "
"membuat batas bawah estimasi sumber daya dapat dicapai.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Diffie-Hellman key exchange and the Digital Signature Algorithm {#diffie-"
"hellman-key-exchange-and-the-digital-signature-algorithm}"
msgstr ""
"Pertukaran kunci Diffie-Hellman dan Algoritma Tanda Tangan Digital {#diffie-"
"hellman-key-exchange-and-the-digital-signature-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous section, we discussed the RSA cryptosystem, whose security "
"is based on the computational hardness of prime factorization. Here, we will"
" discuss two popular asymmetric key cryptographic protocols, [*Diffie-"
"Hellman* key "
"exchange](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman_key_exchange&oldid=1163912552)"
" (DH) and the [*Digital Signature "
"Algorithm*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA), both of which are based on a different mathematical problem, namely "
"the discrete logarithm problem (DLP).\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada bagian sebelumnya, kita membahas kriptosistem RSA, yang keamanannya "
"didasarkan pada kesulitan komputasional dari faktorisasi prima. Di sini, "
"kita akan membahas dua protokol kriptografi kunci asimetris yang populer, "
"pertukaran kunci [*Diffie-"
"Hellman*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman_key_exchange&oldid=1163912552)"
" (DH) dan [*Algoritma Tanda Tangan "
"Digital*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA), keduanya didasarkan pada masalah matematis yang berbeda, yaitu "
"masalah logaritma diskret (DLP).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The discrete logarithm problem {#the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah logaritma diskret {#the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In the following equation we need to find $a$ given only $e$,$M$,$c$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam persamaan berikut kita perlu menemukan $a$ hanya dengan diberikan "
"$e$,$M$,$c$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$a^e$ $mod$ $M = c$\n"
msgstr "$a^e$ $mod$ $M = c$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is believed to be difficult with classic computers due to the use of "
"modulo arithmetic, and therefore is a good mathematical basis for an "
"encryption algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini diyakini sulit dilakukan dengan komputer klasik karena penggunaan "
"aritmetika modulo, dan oleh karena itu merupakan dasar matematis yang baik "
"untuk algoritma enkripsi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is known as the [discrete logarithm "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Discrete_logarithm&oldid=1161792952)"
" (DLP).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini dikenal sebagai [masalah logaritma "
"diskret](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Discrete_logarithm&oldid=1161792952)"
" (DLP).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Mathematical details of the discrete logarithm problem {#mathematical-"
"details-of-the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Detail matematis dari masalah logaritma diskret {#mathematical-details-of-"
"the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The DLP is typically framed in the context of <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Group where all elements are generated by repeatedly applying a"
" single element, known as a generator. This process creates a cycle of "
"elements that closes upon itself.\">cyclic groups</DefinitionTooltip> and is"
" stated as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"DLP biasanya dirumuskan dalam konteks <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Group "
"where all elements are generated by repeatedly applying a single element, "
"known as a generator. This process creates a cycle of elements that closes "
"upon itself.\">grup siklik</DefinitionTooltip> dan dinyatakan sebagai "
"berikut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider a [cyclic "
"group](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cyclic_group&oldid=1150017831)"
" $G$ generated by a group element $g \\in G$ and given an arbitrary element "
"$h \\in G$, find an integer $k$ such that $h = g^{k}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan sebuah [grup "
"siklik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cyclic_group&oldid=1150017831)"
" $G$ yang dibangkitkan oleh elemen grup $g \\in G$ dan diberikan elemen "
"sembarang $h \\in G$, temukan bilangan bulat $k$ sehingga $h = g^{k}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here the integer $k \\equiv log_{g}h$ is the discrete logarithm. The cyclic "
"property of $G$ guarantees that for every $h$, a valid integer $k$ exists.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini bilangan bulat $k \\equiv log_{g}h$ adalah logaritma diskret. Sifat "
"siklik dari $G$ menjamin bahwa untuk setiap $h$, bilangan bulat $k$ yang "
"valid ada.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For cryptography, the DLP on the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The set of "
"integers modulo a prime number, where the group operation is modular "
"multiplication. Elements in the multiplicative group are chosen in such a "
"way that they are coprime to the modulus, ensuring that each element has a "
"unique multiplicative inverse within the group.\">multiplicative "
"group</DefinitionTooltip> of integers modulo a prime number $p$ denoted "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ turns out to be useful. The elements of "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ are congruence classes labeled by integers "
"modulo $p$ that are coprime to $p$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk kriptografi, DLP pada <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The set of "
"integers modulo a prime number, where the group operation is modular "
"multiplication. Elements in the multiplicative group are chosen in such a "
"way that they are coprime to the modulus, ensuring that each element has a "
"unique multiplicative inverse within the group.\">grup "
"multiplikatif</DefinitionTooltip> dari bilangan bulat modulo bilangan prima "
"$p$ yang dilambangkan $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ ternyata berguna. Elemen "
"dari $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ adalah kelas kongruensi yang diberi label "
"dengan bilangan bulat modulo $p$ yang koprima terhadap $p$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For example:\n"
msgstr "Misalnya:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_5)^{\\times} = "
"\\{[1],[2],[3],[4]\\}~\\mathrm{and}~(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times} = "
"\\{[1],[2],[3],[4],[5],[6]\\} $\n"
msgstr ""
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_5)^{\\times} = "
"\\{[1],[2],[3],[4]\\}~\\mathrm{and}~(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times} = "
"\\{[1],[2],[3],[4],[5],[6]\\} $\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation of multiplication $(\\times)$ on these groups is simply "
"ordinary integer multiplication followed by reduction modulo $p$ and "
"exponentiation by an integer $k$ is just repeated multiplication $k$ times "
"and reduction modulo $p$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi perkalian $(\\times)$ pada grup-grup ini hanyalah perkalian bilangan"
" bulat biasa diikuti dengan reduksi modulo $p$ dan eksponensiasi oleh "
"bilangan bulat $k$ hanyalah perkalian berulang sebanyak $k$ kali dan reduksi"
" modulo $p$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let's illustrate an instance of the DLP on $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita ilustrasikan sebuah contoh DLP pada $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This multiplicative group has two generators ${[3],[5]}$ also known as "
"primitive roots. We will use $[5]$ as the generator; that is, generate every"
" element of $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ using successive integer powers of "
"5.\n"
msgstr ""
"Grup multiplikatif ini memiliki dua generator ${[3],[5]}$ yang juga dikenal "
"sebagai akar primitif. Kita akan menggunakan $[5]$ sebagai generator; yaitu,"
" membangkitkan setiap elemen dari $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ menggunakan "
"pangkat bilangan bulat berturut-turut dari 5.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that in modulo 7 arithmetic, raising 5 to successive integer powers "
"yields every element of $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ exactly once before the "
"cycle repeats indefinitely with a period $p-1 =6$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita melihat bahwa dalam aritmetika modulo 7, memangkatkan 5 dengan pangkat "
"bilangan bulat berturut-turut menghasilkan setiap elemen dari "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ tepat sekali sebelum siklus berulang tanpa batas"
" dengan periode $p-1 =6$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "So the DLP on $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ with generator [5] is:\n"
msgstr "Jadi DLP pada $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ dengan generator [5] adalah:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ \\mathrm{Given}~h \\in (\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times} \\mathrm{, find~} k "
"\\mathrm{~such~that~} 5^{k} \\equiv h~(mod~7)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"$ \\mathrm{Given}~h \\in (\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times} \\mathrm{, find~} k "
"\\mathrm{~such~that~} 5^{k} \\equiv h~(mod~7)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "From the above Python cell output we see that:\n"
msgstr "Dari output sel Python di atas kita melihat bahwa:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$h = 2 \\implies k=4 \\mathrm{~or~}  4 = log_5(2) (mod~7)$\n"
msgstr "$h = 2 \\implies k=4 \\mathrm{~or~}  4 = log_5(2) (mod~7)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$h = 6 \\implies k=3 \\mathrm{~or~}  3 = log_5(6) (mod~7)$\n"
msgstr "$h = 6 \\implies k=3 \\mathrm{~or~}  3 = log_5(6) (mod~7)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In ordinary real number arithmetic, exponentiation is a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A behavior or relationship that consistently moves in a single "
"direction without reversals; for example in a monotonically increasing "
"function, values consistently increase.\">monotonic</DefinitionTooltip> "
"function and finding the logarithm of any number to any base is "
"computationally easy. In contrast, as is apparent from the simple "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ example above, modular exponentiation is non-"
"monotonic, and even though it is periodic with period $p-1$, it is otherwise"
" highly nontrivial. So computing its inverse, the discrete logarithm turns "
"out to be inefficient for large $p$ on classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam aritmetika bilangan real biasa, eksponensiasi adalah fungsi yang "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A behavior or relationship that consistently"
" moves in a single direction without reversals; for example in a "
"monotonically increasing function, values consistently "
"increase.\">monoton</DefinitionTooltip> dan menemukan logaritma dari "
"bilangan apa pun ke basis apa pun secara komputasi mudah. Sebaliknya, "
"seperti yang terlihat jelas dari contoh $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ "
"sederhana di atas, eksponensiasi modular bersifat non-monoton, dan meskipun "
"bersifat periodik dengan periode $p-1$, selebihnya sangat tidak trivial. "
"Jadi menghitung inversnya, logaritma diskret, ternyata tidak efisien untuk "
"$p$ yang besar pada komputer klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This observation underpins both Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange and the "
"Digital Signature Algorithm (DSA), which are discussed in the next "
"section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengamatan ini menjadi dasar dari pertukaran kunci Diffie-Hellman (DH) dan "
"Algoritma Tanda Tangan Digital (DSA), yang dibahas di bagian berikutnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The DLP can be extended to cyclic subgroups as follows:\n"
msgstr "DLP dapat diperluas ke subgrup siklik sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ defined above and an element $g \\in "
"(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ of prime order $r$ that is, $g^r \\equiv 1 "
"(~mod~p)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ yang didefinisikan di atas dan "
"sebuah elemen $g \\in (\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ berorde prima $r$ yaitu, "
"$g^r \\equiv 1 (~mod~p)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The set of integer powers of $g$: $\\{g^k~(mod~p) | 1 \\le k \\le r\\} = "
"\\langle g \\rangle$ is a cyclic subgroup of $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ "
"with group order $r$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Himpunan pangkat bilangan bulat dari $g$: $\\{g^k~(mod~p) | 1 \\le k \\le "
"r\\} = \\langle g \\rangle$ adalah subgrup siklik dari "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ dengan orde grup $r$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A DLP can be specified on $\\langle g \\rangle$ by choosing a $h \\in "
"\\langle g \\rangle$ and asking for $1 \\le a \\le r$ such that $ "
"g^a~(mod~p) = h$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebuah DLP dapat ditentukan pada $\\langle g \\rangle$ dengan memilih $h "
"\\in \\\\langle g \\rangle$ dan meminta $1 \\le a \\le r$ sehingga $ "
"g^a~(mod~p) = h$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Diffie-Hellman key exchange {#diffie-hellman-key-exchange}"
msgstr "Pertukaran kunci Diffie-Hellman {#diffie-hellman-key-exchange}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In 1976, [Whitfield Diffie and Martin Hellman proposed a key exchange "
"protocol](https://doi.org/10.1109/TIT.1976.1055638) to enable the creation "
"of a shared secret key over insecure communication channels. The secret key "
"could then be used by parties sharing it for symmetric encryption. The "
"algorithm relies on the DLP.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada tahun 1976, [Whitfield Diffie dan Martin Hellman mengusulkan protokol "
"pertukaran kunci](https://doi.org/10.1109/TIT.1976.1055638) untuk "
"memungkinkan pembuatan kunci rahasia bersama melalui saluran komunikasi yang"
" tidak aman. Kunci rahasia tersebut kemudian dapat digunakan oleh pihak-"
"pihak yang berbagi untuk enkripsi simetris. Algoritma ini bergantung pada "
"DLP.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 1. Diffie-Hellman key exchange](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/key_exchange_dh.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 1. Diffie-Hellman key exchange](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/key_exchange_dh.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 1. Diffie-Hellman key exchange*\n"
msgstr "*Gambar 1. Pertukaran kunci Diffie-Hellman*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: <Accordion>
# <AccordionItem title="Detail matematis dari pert
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: Dengan Alice dan
# Bob sebagai dua pihak yang berkomunikasi, p
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of Diffie-Hellman key "
"exchange\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With Alice and Bob being the two parties communicating, the protocol works "
"as follows:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, Alice and Bob agree on a large prime number $p$ and a primitive root "
"or generator $a$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, Alice dan Bob sepakat tentang bilangan prima besar $p$ dan akar "
"primitif atau generator $a$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice chooses a secret exponent $k_A$ randomly with $1 \\le k_A \\le "
"p-2$ and calculates $h_A = a^{k_A}~(mod~p)$. $k_A, h_A$ are Alice's  private"
" and public keys respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Alice memilih eksponen rahasia $k_A$ secara acak dengan $1 \\le "
"k_A \\le p-2$ dan menghitung $h_A = a^{k_A}~(mod~p)$. $k_A, h_A$ masing-"
"masing adalah kunci privat dan publik Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Bob chooses a secret exponent $k_B$ randomly with  $1 \\le k_B \\le "
"p-2$ and calculates $h_B = a^{k_B}~(mod~p)$. $k_B, h_B$ are Bob's  private "
"and public keys respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, Bob memilih eksponen rahasia $k_B$ secara acak dengan $1 \\le "
"k_B \\le p-2$ dan menghitung $h_B = a^{k_B}~(mod~p)$. $k_B, h_B$ masing-"
"masing adalah kunci privat dan publik Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice sends Bob $h_A$ and Bob sends Alice $h_B$ over a reliable but "
"not necessarily secure channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Alice mengirim $h_A$ ke Bob dan Bob mengirim $h_B$ ke Alice "
"melalui saluran yang andal namun tidak harus aman.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice then uses the $h_B$ she received to compute the shared secret "
"key $ \\kappa = h_B^{k_A}~(mod~p)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lalu, Alice menggunakan $h_B$ yang diterimanya untuk menghitung kunci "
"rahasia bersama $ \\kappa = h_B^{k_A}~(mod~p)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob meanwhile uses the $h_A$ he received to compute the shared "
"secret key $ \\kappa = h_A^{k_B}~(mod~p)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terakhir, Bob sementara itu menggunakan $h_A$ yang diterimanya untuk "
"menghitung kunci rahasia bersama $ \\kappa = h_A^{k_B}~(mod~p)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "With this protocol,\n"
msgstr "Dengan protokol ini,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob are guaranteed to end up with the same secret key $\\kappa$ "
"because $h_B^{k_A}~(mod~p) = (a^{k_B})^{k_A}~(mod~p) = a^{k_A k_B}~(mod~p) ="
" (a^{k_A})^{k_B}~(mod~p) = h_A^{k_B}~(mod~p) $.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice dan Bob dijamin mendapatkan kunci rahasia yang sama $\\kappa$ karena "
"$h_B^{k_A}~(mod~p) = (a^{k_B})^{k_A}~(mod~p) = a^{k_A k_B}~(mod~p) = "
"(a^{k_A})^{k_B}~(mod~p) = h_A^{k_B}~(mod~p) $.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A third party that intercepts $h_A$ or $h_B$ cannot construct the secret key"
" $\\kappa$ because they do not have access to $k_B$ or $k_A$ respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pihak ketiga yang mencegat $h_A$ atau $h_B$ tidak dapat membuat kunci "
"rahasia $\\kappa$ karena mereka tidak memiliki akses ke $k_B$ atau $k_A$ "
"masing-masing.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Extracting $k_A$ or $k_B$ using the public information $a$, $p$, $h_A$ and "
"$h_B$ is computationally hard as it is equivalent to solving the DLP on "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengekstrak $k_A$ atau $k_B$ menggunakan informasi publik $a$, $p$, $h_A$ "
"dan $h_B$ secara komputasi sulit karena setara dengan memecahkan DLP pada "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Illustration of the Diffie-Hellman protocol in Python {#illustration-of-the-"
"diffie-hellman-protocol-in-python}"
msgstr ""
"Ilustrasi protokol Diffie-Hellman dalam Python {#illustration-of-the-diffie-"
"hellman-protocol-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's look at a simple example of the DH protocol in Python using small "
"prime numbers:\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita lihat contoh sederhana protokol DH dalam Python menggunakan "
"bilangan prima kecil:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 1:** Alice and Bob agree on a prime $p$ and a primitive root $a$. "
"Let's choose $p=11, a=7$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 1:** Alice dan Bob sepakat tentang prima $p$ dan akar primitif "
"$a$. Mari pilih $p=11, a=7$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Steps 2, 3:** Alice chooses a secret exponent $k_A$ and calculates $h_A = "
"a^{k_A}~(mod~p)$. Similarly, Bob chooses a secret exponent $k_B$ and "
"calculates $h_B = a^{k_B}~(mod~p)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 2, 3:** Alice memilih eksponen rahasia $k_A$ dan menghitung $h_A ="
" a^{k_A}~(mod~p)$. Demikian pula, Bob memilih eksponen rahasia $k_B$ dan "
"menghitung $h_B = a^{k_B}~(mod~p)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 4:** The two parties broadcast their public keys $h_A$ and $h_B$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 4:** Kedua pihak menyiarkan kunci publik mereka $h_A$ dan $h_B$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Steps 5, 6:** Each party combines their private key with the other party's"
" public key to create the shared secret key.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 5, 6:** Setiap pihak menggabungkan kunci privatnya dengan kunci "
"publik pihak lain untuk membuat kunci rahasia bersama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob can now use the shared secret key for symmetric encryption.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice dan Bob sekarang dapat menggunakan kunci rahasia bersama untuk "
"enkripsi simetris.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Security of Diffie-Hellman key exchange {#security-of-diffie-hellman-key-"
"exchange}"
msgstr ""
"Keamanan pertukaran kunci Diffie-Hellman {#security-of-diffie-hellman-key-"
"exchange}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As noted above, the security of DH is predicated on the computational "
"difficulty of solving the DLP with large primes $p$. In typical "
"applications, NIST recommends 2048- or 3072-bit prime integers for DH key "
"exchange, which is considered sufficiently secure against attempts to solve "
"the DLP using classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang disebutkan di atas, keamanan DH bergantung pada kesulitan "
"komputasional dalam memecahkan DLP dengan prima besar $p$. Dalam aplikasi "
"tipikal, NIST merekomendasikan bilangan prima 2048- atau 3072-bit untuk "
"pertukaran kunci DH, yang dianggap cukup aman terhadap upaya memecahkan DLP "
"menggunakan komputer klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Man-in-the-middle (MITM) attacks**: The fact that DH is an interactive "
"scheme where the shared secret depends on combining one party's private key "
"with the other party's public key makes it vulnerable to a so-called *Man-"
"in-the-middle (MITM)* attack.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Serangan man-in-the-middle (MITM)**: Fakta bahwa DH adalah skema "
"interaktif di mana rahasia bersama bergantung pada penggabungan kunci privat"
" satu pihak dengan kunci publik pihak lain membuatnya rentan terhadap "
"serangan yang disebut *Man-in-the-middle (MITM)*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: <Accordion>
# <AccordionItem title="Detail matematis keamanan
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of DH security and MITM "
"attacks\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this scenario, a third party — say, Eve — intercepts the public keys "
"$h_A, h_B$ during transmission and substitutes her own public key $h_E$ for "
"each of $h_A$ and $h_B$ before forwarding them along to Bob and Alice, "
"respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam skenario ini, pihak ketiga — misalnya, Eve — mencegat kunci publik "
"$h_A, h_B$ selama transmisi dan menggantikan kunci publiknya sendiri $h_E$ "
"untuk masing-masing $h_A$ dan $h_B$ sebelum meneruskannya ke Bob dan "
"Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, instead of using $h_B$ to create her shared secret, Alice will use "
"$h_E$ while thinking that she is using Bob's public key. Similarly, instead "
"of using $h_A$ to create his shared secret, Bob will use $h_E$ while "
"thinking that he is using Alice's public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, alih-alih menggunakan $h_B$ untuk membuat rahasia bersamanya, "
"Alice akan menggunakan $h_E$ sambil berpikir bahwa dia menggunakan kunci "
"publik Bob. Demikian pula, alih-alih menggunakan $h_A$ untuk membuat rahasia"
" bersamanya, Bob akan menggunakan $h_E$ sambil berpikir bahwa dia "
"menggunakan kunci publik Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because $h_E$ was used to create Alice's (Bob's) shared secret, plain text "
"encrypted by Alice (Bob) can be decrypted by Eve.\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena $h_E$ digunakan untuk membuat rahasia bersama Alice (Bob), teks biasa"
" yang dienkripsi oleh Alice (Bob) dapat didekripsi oleh Eve.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, DH key exchange is typically used in conjunction with a digital "
"signature algorithm to ensure that each party uses an authenticated public "
"key for creating their shared secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan demikian, pertukaran kunci DH biasanya digunakan bersama dengan "
"algoritma tanda tangan digital untuk memastikan bahwa setiap pihak "
"menggunakan kunci publik yang telah diautentikasi untuk membuat rahasia "
"bersamanya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Digital Signature Algorithm (DSA) {#the-digital-signature-algorithm-dsa}"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Tanda Tangan Digital (DSA) {#the-digital-signature-algorithm-dsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Even though generic cryptosystems like [RSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_(cryptosystem)&oldid=1163962255) provide digital signature functionality, in 1994 NIST adopted a specialized signature scheme based on modular exponentiation and the discrete logarithm problem as the federal standard for digital signatures. This scheme, which came to be known simply as the [*Digital Signature Algorithm*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522) (DSA), involves four distinct phases:\n"
"1. **Key generation**:\n"
msgstr ""
"Meskipun sistem kriptografi generik seperti "
"[RSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_(cryptosystem)&oldid=1163962255)"
" menyediakan fungsionalitas tanda tangan digital, pada tahun 1994 NIST "
"mengadopsi skema tanda tangan khusus berdasarkan eksponensiasi modular dan "
"masalah logaritma diskret sebagai standar federal untuk tanda tangan "
"digital. Skema ini, yang kemudian dikenal sederhana sebagai [*Algoritma "
"Tanda Tangan "
"Digital*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA), melibatkan empat fase yang berbeda:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   DSA keys are generated from:\n"
"     - 2 primes that meet certain rules\n"
"       -   $p$ - typically 256 bits (we'll call this length $N$)\n"
"       -   $q$ - typically 3072 bits (we'll call this length $L$)\n"
"     - A cryptographic hash function that will convert from strings of length $L$ to $N$\n"
"     - An additional Parameters $g$ (see details below)\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kunci DSA dibuat dari:\n"
"     - 2 prima yang memenuhi aturan tertentu\n"
"       -   $p$ - biasanya 256 bit (kita sebut panjang ini $N$)\n"
"       -   $q$ - biasanya 3072 bit (kita sebut panjang ini $L$)\n"
"     - Fungsi hash kriptografi yang akan mengkonversi dari string dengan panjang $L$ ke $N$\n"
"     - Parameter tambahan $g$ (lihat detail di bawah)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   From this we choose a random number $x$ as private key, and are able to "
"calculate a public key $y$\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dari ini kita memilih bilangan acak $x$ sebagai kunci privat, dan dapat "
"menghitung kunci publik $y$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of key generation\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Detail matematis pembuatan kunci\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Parameter generation:** Mathematically, DSA involves a cyclic subgroup of "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ generated by an element $g$ of prime order q < "
"p. The first step in the DSA is therefore to select two primes p, q to set "
"up the necessary mathematical structures.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pembuatan parameter:** Secara matematis, DSA melibatkan subgrup siklik "
"dari $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ yang dibangkitkan oleh elemen $g$ berorde "
"prima q < p. Langkah pertama dalam DSA oleh karena itu adalah memilih dua "
"prima p, q untuk menyiapkan struktur matematis yang diperlukan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose an $N$-bit prime $q$.\n"
msgstr "Pilih prima $q$ berukuran $N$-bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose an $L$-bit prime $p$ such that $p-1$ is a multiple of $q$. The choice"
" of $p$ specifies the group $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih prima $p$ berukuran $L$-bit sedemikian sehingga $p-1$ adalah kelipatan"
" dari $q$. Pilihan $p$ menentukan grup $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pick an integer $1 < h < p-1$ at random and compute $g = h^{(p-1)/q}~mod~p$."
" If $g=1$ which happens rarely, try another h.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih bilangan bulat $1 < h < p-1$ secara acak dan hitung $g = "
"h^{(p-1)/q}~mod~p$. Jika $g=1$ yang jarang terjadi, coba $h$ yang lain.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Verify that $g^q~mod~p = 1$. g is thus a generator of a cyclic subgroup "
"$\\langle g \\rangle$ of $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ of prime order q.\n"
msgstr ""
"Verifikasi bahwa $g^q~mod~p = 1$. Dengan demikian g adalah generator dari "
"subgrup siklik $\\langle g \\rangle$ dari $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ "
"berorde prima q.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     The parameters $(q, p, g)$ specify an instance of the algorithm and are"
" public information. Typically, $ N \\sim 256$ and $L \\sim 3072$ in "
"realistic applications.\n"
msgstr ""
"     Parameter $(q, p, g)$ menentukan sebuah contoh algoritma dan merupakan "
"informasi publik. Biasanya, $ N \\sim 256$ dan $L \\sim 3072$ dalam aplikasi"
" nyata.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     The protocol also requires a cryptographic hash function $H : "
"\\{0,1\\}^L \\rightarrow \\{0, 1\\}^N$ that maps binary $L$-bit strings to "
"$N$-bit strings, for example, SHA-256.\n"
msgstr ""
"     Protokol ini juga memerlukan fungsi hash kriptografi $H : \\{0,1\\}^L "
"\\rightarrow \\{0, 1\\}^N$ yang memetakan string biner $L$-bit ke string "
"$N$-bit, misalnya, SHA-256.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key-pair generation:** The signer needs to generate a key pair on their "
"end.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pembuatan pasangan kunci:** Penanda tangan perlu membuat pasangan kunci di"
" pihaknya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose a random secret integer $ x \\in \\{1,2...q-1\\}$. $x$ is the private"
" key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih bilangan bulat rahasia acak $ x \\in \\{1,2...q-1\\}$. $x$ adalah "
"kunci privat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generate $ y = g^{x}~mod~p$. $y$ is the signer's public key.\n"
msgstr "Hasilkan $ y = g^{x}~mod~p$. $y$ adalah kunci publik penanda tangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The following information is shared with anyone who wishes to validate a signature\n"
"   - The parameters used $(p,q,g)$ which describe the algorithm\n"
"   - The hash function $H$\n"
"   - the public key $y$\n"
"1. **Signing:**\n"
msgstr ""
"   Informasi berikut dibagikan kepada siapa pun yang ingin memvalidasi tanda tangan\n"
"   - Parameter yang digunakan $(p,q,g)$ yang mendeskripsikan algoritma\n"
"   - Fungsi hash $H$\n"
"   - Kunci publik $y$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The signer can now sign a message $m$. The resulting signature is $(r,s)$\n"
msgstr ""
"Penanda tangan sekarang dapat menandatangani pesan $m$. Tanda tangan yang "
"dihasilkan adalah $(r,s)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The message and signature are both now sent to the recipient\n"
msgstr "Pesan dan tanda tangan keduanya sekarang dikirim ke penerima\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of signing a message\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Detail matematis penandatanganan pesan\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   The signer signs a message $m$ as follows:\n"
msgstr "   Penanda tangan menandatangani pesan $m$ sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a secret integer k at random from $\\{1,2...q-1\\}$\n"
msgstr "Pilih bilangan bulat rahasia k secara acak dari $\\{1,2...q-1\\}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute $r = (g^k~mod~p)~mod~q$. In the rare instance when $r=0$, try "
"another random k.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hitung $r = (g^k~mod~p)~mod~q$. Dalam kasus langka ketika $r=0$, coba k acak"
" yang lain.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute $s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr))~mod~q$. In a rare instances if $s=0$, try "
"another random k.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hitung $s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr))~mod~q$. Dalam kasus langka jika $s=0$, coba"
" k acak yang lain.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The signature is the tuple $(r, s)$.\n"
msgstr "Tanda tangan adalah tupel $(r, s)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The signer transmits the message $m$ as well as the signature $(r,s)$ to the"
" verifier.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penanda tangan mentransmisikan pesan $m$ beserta tanda tangan $(r,s)$ ke "
"verifikator.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Because both $r, s$ are integers, modulo $q$ the signature size is on the"
" order of $N$-bits and not the longer $L$-bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Karena $r, s$ keduanya adalah bilangan bulat, modulo $q$ ukuran tanda "
"tangan berada dalam urutan $N$-bit dan bukan $L$-bit yang lebih panjang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"2. **Verification:**\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The recipient now wishes to verify the authenticity of the sender.\n"
"   They have access to the public information $(q, p, g, H, y, (r,s), m)$\n"
"   They can execute a calculation which proves that the sender had access to the private key $x$\n"
msgstr ""
"   Penerima sekarang ingin memverifikasi keaslian pengirim.\n"
"   Mereka memiliki akses ke informasi publik $(q, p, g, H, y, (r,s), m)$\n"
"   Mereka dapat menjalankan kalkulasi yang membuktikan bahwa pengirim memiliki akses ke kunci privat $x$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   and seeks to ascertain that the signer is someone with access to the "
"private key $x$.\n"
msgstr ""
"   dan berupaya memastikan bahwa penanda tangan adalah seseorang dengan "
"akses ke kunci privat $x$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of DSA verification scheme\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Detail matematis skema verifikasi DSA\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Verify that $0 \\lt r \\lt q$ and $0 \\lt s \\lt q$, that is, $r, s$ are "
"valid modulo~q integers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Verifikasi bahwa $0 \\lt r \\lt q$ dan $0 \\lt s \\lt q$, yaitu, $r, s$ "
"adalah bilangan bulat modulo~q yang valid.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $w = s^{-1}~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Hitung $w = s^{-1}~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $u_1 = H(m)w~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Hitung $u_1 = H(m)w~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $u_2 = rw~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Hitung $u_2 = rw~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $v = (g^{u_1}y^{u_2}~mod~p)~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Hitung $v = (g^{u_1}y^{u_2}~mod~p)~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The signature is verified if $v = r$.\n"
msgstr "Tanda tangan diverifikasi jika $v = r$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For legitimate signatures, the correctness of the DSA algorithm is easily"
" demonstrated as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Untuk tanda tangan yang sah, kebenaran algoritma DSA mudah ditunjukkan "
"sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the signer's end: $s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr))~mod~q \\implies k = ((H(m) + "
"xr)s^{-1})~mod~q $\n"
msgstr ""
"Di pihak penanda tangan: $s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr))~mod~q \\implies k = "
"((H(m) + xr)s^{-1})~mod~q $\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Considering the right-hand side of the latter equality, a verifier can "
"compute $s^{-1}, H(m)$ because $s, q, m, H$ are public information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mempertimbangkan sisi kanan dari kesamaan tersebut, verifikator dapat "
"menghitung $s^{-1}, H(m)$ karena $s, q, m, H$ adalah informasi publik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, the verifier computes $w = s^{-1}~mod~q$ and $u_1 = H(m)w~mod~q = "
"H(m)s^{-1}~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan demikian, verifikator menghitung $w = s^{-1}~mod~q$ dan $u_1 = "
"H(m)w~mod~q = H(m)s^{-1}~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The verifier also computes $u_2 = rw~mod~q = rs^{-1}~mod~q$ as $r$ is also "
"public.\n"
msgstr ""
"Verifikator juga menghitung $u_2 = rw~mod~q = rs^{-1}~mod~q$ karena $r$ juga"
" merupakan informasi publik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Note that $k = (u_1 + xu_2)~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahwa $k = (u_1 + xu_2)~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, a verifier does not have access to $x$ as it is the signer's "
"private key, so $k$ itself cannot be directly computed.  - The scheme "
"instead relies on the fact that even as the verifier cannot compute $k$, "
"with a legitimate signer, the verifier should instead be able to re-compute "
"$(g^k~mod~p)~mod~q = r$ with the help of the signer's public key $y = "
"g^{x}~mod~p$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Namun, verifikator tidak memiliki akses ke $x$ karena itu adalah kunci "
"privat penanda tangan, sehingga $k$ sendiri tidak dapat dihitung secara "
"langsung.  - Skema ini mengandalkan fakta bahwa meskipun verifikator tidak "
"dapat menghitung $k$, dengan penanda tangan yang sah, verifikator seharusnya"
" bisa menghitung ulang $(g^k~mod~p)~mod~q = r$ dengan bantuan kunci publik "
"penanda tangan $y = g^{x}~mod~p$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, the verifier computes $v = (g^{u_1}y^{u_2}~mod~p)~mod~q = "
"(g^{u_1}g^{xu_2}~mod~p)mod~q = (g^{u_1+xu_2}~mod~p)mod~q = "
"(g^k~mod~p)mod~q$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, verifikator menghitung $v = (g^{u_1}y^{u_2}~mod~p)~mod~q = "
"(g^{u_1}g^{xu_2}~mod~p)mod~q = (g^{u_1+xu_2}~mod~p)mod~q = "
"(g^k~mod~p)mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last equality follows because $g$ has order $q$ and establishes $v = r$ "
"for valid signatures.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kesamaan terakhir mengikuti karena $g$ berorde $q$ dan menetapkan $v = r$ "
"untuk tanda tangan yang valid.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Illustration of the DSA in Python {#illustration-of-the-dsa-in-python}"
msgstr "Ilustrasi DSA dalam Python {#illustration-of-the-dsa-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this example, we'll use small primes to illustrate the DSA process in a "
"scenario where Alice sends a signed message to Bob. We'll use small integers"
" in this example. A real-world scenario would employ much larger primes on "
"the order of 2048-3072 bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini, kita akan menggunakan prima kecil untuk mengilustrasikan "
"proses DSA dalam skenario di mana Alice mengirimkan pesan bertanda tangan ke"
" Bob. Kita akan menggunakan bilangan bulat kecil dalam contoh ini. Skenario "
"dunia nyata akan menggunakan prima yang jauh lebih besar dalam urutan "
"2048-3072 bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"You can try rerunning this example with different values to see how the algorithm behaves, but ensure you start running from the first cell in this section.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Kamu bisa mencoba menjalankan ulang contoh ini dengan nilai yang berbeda untuk melihat bagaimana algoritma berperilaku, tetapi pastikan kamu mulai menjalankan dari sel pertama di bagian ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We start by importing necessary libraries and choosing our parameters.\n"
"The integer parameters $p$, $q$, $g$ are public information, and satisfy the following rules:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mulai dengan mengimpor library yang diperlukan dan memilih parameter kita.\n"
"Parameter bilangan bulat $p$, $q$, $g$ adalah informasi publik, dan memenuhi aturan berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$p$, $q$ are both prime\n"
msgstr "$p$, $q$ keduanya prima\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$(p-1) \\mod\\ q = 0$\n"
msgstr "$(p-1) \\mod\\ q = 0$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$g \\ge 2$\n"
msgstr "$g \\ge 2$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$g \\le (p-2)$\n"
msgstr "$g \\le (p-2)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$g^{(p-1)/q} \\mod\\ p \\neq 1$\n"
msgstr "$g^{(p-1)/q} \\mod\\ p \\neq 1$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next the signer, Alice, generates her private key.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya penanda tangan, Alice, membuat kunci privatnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The private key, k (`alice-private-key` in the python code) must satisfy:\n"
" - $k \\ge 2$\n"
" - $k \\le (q-1)$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci privat, k (`alice-private-key` dalam kode Python) harus memenuhi:\n"
" - $k \\ge 2$\n"
" - $k \\le (q-1)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice keeps her private key secret.\n"
msgstr "Alice menyimpan kunci privatnya sebagai rahasia.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Alice computes her public key using modular exponentiation. Inverting "
"this step to recover the private key is an instance of the DLP, so difficult"
" to compute on classical computers where large primes are used.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, Alice menghitung kunci publiknya menggunakan eksponensiasi "
"modular. Membalikkan langkah ini untuk memulihkan kunci privat adalah sebuah"
" contoh DLP, jadi sulit dihitung pada komputer klasik ketika prima besar "
"digunakan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From the math explanation above, we know is this can be calculated using the"
" formula:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dari penjelasan matematis di atas, kita tahu ini dapat dihitung menggunakan "
"rumus:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$y = g^{x} \\mod\\ p$\n"
msgstr "$y = g^{x} \\mod\\ p$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As usual, Alice makes her public key available over a not-necessarily secret"
" channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti biasa, Alice membuat kunci publiknya tersedia melalui saluran yang "
"tidak harus bersifat rahasia.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now Alice can sign a message.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang Alice dapat menandatangani sebuah pesan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the digital signature scheme, we need to generate a hash $H(m)$ of the "
"message $m$ to be signed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk skema tanda tangan digital, kita perlu membuat hash $H(m)$ dari pesan "
"$m$ yang akan ditandatangani.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's assume Alice and Bob agree to use a particular hashing algorithm with "
"hash length $N$ equal to the number of bits in $q$. In this simple example, "
"we will bound the outputs of our mock hash function by $q$. The hash "
"function here is trivial, simply generating a random integer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalkan Alice dan Bob sepakat untuk menggunakan algoritma hashing tertentu "
"dengan panjang hash $N$ sama dengan jumlah bit dalam $q$. Dalam contoh "
"sederhana ini, kita akan membatasi output dari fungsi hash tiruan kita "
"dengan $q$. Fungsi hash di sini sangat sederhana, hanya menghasilkan "
"bilangan bulat acak.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Alice needs to generate a random per-message secret number $k$ as well"
" as its multiplicative inverse modulo $q$ to compute the signature.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, Alice perlu membuat bilangan rahasia acak per-pesan $k$ beserta"
" invers perkalian modulo $q$ untuk menghitung tanda tangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A simple brute-force algorithm can be used to compute the modular inverse. "
"However it's better to use one of the built-in Python function `pow` as "
"shown below\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma brute-force sederhana dapat digunakan untuk menghitung invers "
"modular. Namun lebih baik menggunakan salah satu fungsi bawaan Python `pow` "
"seperti yang ditunjukkan di bawah ini\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice can now compute the signature.\n"
msgstr "Alice sekarang dapat menghitung tanda tangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$r = (g^{k} \\mod p) \\mod\\ q$\n"
msgstr "$r = (g^{k} \\mod p) \\mod\\ q$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr)) \\mod q$\n"
msgstr "$s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr)) \\mod q$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that there are some particular conditions that will require us to "
"choose a different value for $k$ in the case where either $r$ or $s$ compute"
" to $0$. In this case we will generate a new value and repeat.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa ada beberapa kondisi tertentu yang akan mengharuskan kita "
"memilih nilai $k$ yang berbeda dalam kasus di mana $r$ atau $s$ menghasilkan"
" nilai $0$. Dalam kasus ini kita akan membuat nilai baru dan mengulangi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice broadcasts the message and her signature to the receiver or verifier, "
"Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice menyiarkan pesan dan tanda tangannya ke penerima atau verifikator, "
"Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bob has previously intercepted Alice's public key and can now verify the "
"signature to authenticate her message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bob sebelumnya telah mendapatkan kunci publik Alice dan sekarang dapat "
"memverifikasi tanda tangan untuk mengautentikasi pesannya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To do so, he performs some checks, and then re-generates a hash of Alice's broadcast message and computes the auxiliary quantities $w, u_1, u_2$ and $v$.\n"
"- $0 < r < q$\n"
"- $0 < s < q$\n"
"- $w = s^{-1} \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $u_{1} = H(m) . w \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $u_{2} = r . w \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $v = (g^{u1}y^{u2} \\mod\\ p) \\mod\\ q$\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk melakukannya, ia melakukan beberapa pemeriksaan, kemudian membuat ulang hash dari pesan siaran Alice dan menghitung kuantitas tambahan $w, u_1, u_2$ dan $v$.\n"
"- $0 < r < q$\n"
"- $0 < s < q$\n"
"- $w = s^{-1} \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $u_{1} = H(m) . w \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $u_{2} = r . w \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $v = (g^{u1}y^{u2} \\mod\\ p) \\mod\\ q$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob checks if $v$ equals $r$. If they are equal, then the signature"
" is verified.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, Bob memeriksa apakah $v$ sama dengan $r$. Jika keduanya sama, maka"
" tanda tangan diverifikasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Security of the DSA {#security-of-the-dsa}"
msgstr "Keamanan DSA {#security-of-the-dsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With classical computing, the security of the DSA can be influenced by "
"several factors:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan komputasi klasik, keamanan DSA dapat dipengaruhi oleh beberapa "
"faktor:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key size**: As always, key size provides basic protection against brute "
"force attacks. Modern applications that use DSA use key sizes of at least "
"2048 bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ukuran kunci**: Seperti biasa, ukuran kunci memberikan perlindungan dasar "
"terhadap serangan brute force. Aplikasi modern yang menggunakan DSA "
"menggunakan ukuran kunci minimal 2048 bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Quality of $k$**: In DSA, each signature needs a unique, random, and "
"secret $k$ value (see above). The uniqueness, entropy, and secrecy of $k$ "
"are critical, and weakness in any of these aspects could lead to the private"
" key $x$ being compromised. The random number generators used for generating"
" $k$ need to be secure themselves.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kualitas $k$**: Dalam DSA, setiap tanda tangan memerlukan nilai $k$ yang "
"unik, acak, dan rahasia (lihat di atas). Keunikan, entropi, dan kerahasiaan "
"$k$ sangat penting, dan kelemahan dalam salah satu aspek ini dapat "
"menyebabkan kunci privat $x$ dikompromikan. Generator bilangan acak yang "
"digunakan untuk menghasilkan $k$ harus aman sendiri.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Hash function strength**: Since DSA uses a hash function as part of the "
"signature generation and verification process, a weak hash function could "
"compromise the security of the digital signature. For example, the use of "
"SHA-1 with DSA is deprecated and SHA-2 or higher is recommended.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kekuatan fungsi hash**: Karena DSA menggunakan fungsi hash sebagai bagian "
"dari proses pembuatan dan verifikasi tanda tangan, fungsi hash yang lemah "
"dapat membahayakan keamanan tanda tangan digital. Misalnya, penggunaan SHA-1"
" dengan DSA sudah tidak digunakan lagi dan SHA-2 atau yang lebih tinggi "
"direkomendasikan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to these, robust DSA implementation should also guard against "
"other types of attacks that target asymmetric key cryptography as previously"
" outlined.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain itu, implementasi DSA yang kuat juga harus melindungi terhadap jenis "
"serangan lain yang menargetkan kriptografi kunci asimetris seperti yang "
"telah diuraikan sebelumnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Authenticated key exchange with Diffie-Hellman and DSA {#authenticated-key-"
"exchange-with-diffie-hellman-and-dsa}"
msgstr ""
"Pertukaran kunci terotentikasi dengan Diffie-Hellman dan DSA "
"{#authenticated-key-exchange-with-diffie-hellman-and-dsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Modern network security protocols, such as [Transport Layer Security "
"(TLS)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531)"
" and many others, involve combining the functionalities of key exchange and "
"authentication. In the context of Diffie-Hellman, authentication is needed "
"to guard against MITM attacks. In the following code cells, we illustrate an"
" example where Alice and Bob perform an authenticated key exchange by "
"combining the Diffie-Hellman and DSA protocols. For this, we will use the "
"`cryptography` Python library.\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 2. Authenticated key exchange with Diffie-Hellman and "
"DSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/auth_key_exchange.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 2. Authenticated key exchange with Diffie-Hellman and "
"DSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/auth_key_exchange.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"*Gambar 2. Pertukaran kunci terotentikasi dengan Diffie-Hellman dan DSA*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 2. Authenticated key exchange with Diffie-Hellman and DSA*\n"
"First, Alice and Bob agree on a set of DH parameters and generate a set of DH public-private key pairs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, Alice dan Bob sepakat tentang satu set parameter DH dan membuat "
"satu set pasangan kunci publik-privat DH.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The DH public keys are broadcast. Next, both Alice and Bob each generate a "
"separate key pair for use with DSA. These keys will in turn be used to sign "
"the DH public keys to be exchanged.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci publik DH disiarkan. Selanjutnya, Alice dan Bob masing-masing membuat "
"pasangan kunci terpisah untuk digunakan dengan DSA. Kunci-kunci ini pada "
"gilirannya akan digunakan untuk menandatangani kunci publik DH yang akan "
"dipertukarkan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice signs her DH public key using her DSA private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice menandatangani kunci publik DH-nya menggunakan kunci privat DSA-nya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, Bob signs his DH public key using his DSA private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Demikian pula, Bob menandatangani kunci publik DH-nya menggunakan kunci "
"privat DSA-nya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The DH public keys and corresponding signatures are now broadcast by both "
"Alice and Bob. Having received their counterparty's public key and "
"signature, each party then verifies the signature is valid. This way, a MITM"
" attack can be prevented, as Alice, for instance, knows that Bob's DH public"
" key was indeed signed by Bob and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci publik DH dan tanda tangan yang sesuai sekarang disiarkan oleh Alice "
"dan Bob. Setelah menerima kunci publik dan tanda tangan dari pihak lawan, "
"setiap pihak kemudian memverifikasi bahwa tanda tangan tersebut valid. "
"Dengan cara ini, serangan MITM dapat dicegah, karena Alice, misalnya, tahu "
"bahwa kunci publik DH Bob memang ditandatangani oleh Bob dan sebaliknya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Following signature verification, Alice and Bob generate the shared secret, "
"which completes the key exchange.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah verifikasi tanda tangan, Alice dan Bob membuat rahasia bersama, yang"
" menyelesaikan pertukaran kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optionally, for additional security, Alice and Bob can use a specialized key"
" derivation function such as *HKDF* to generate a more secure symmetric key "
"from their shared secret using *key stretching* techniques.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai opsional, untuk keamanan tambahan, Alice dan Bob dapat menggunakan "
"fungsi derivasi kunci khusus seperti *HKDF* untuk menghasilkan kunci "
"simetris yang lebih aman dari rahasia bersama mereka menggunakan teknik *key"
" stretching*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Breaking Diffie-Hellman and DSA {#breaking-diffie-hellman-and-dsa}"
msgstr "Membobol Diffie-Hellman dan DSA {#breaking-diffie-hellman-and-dsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both the [Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman_key_exchange&oldid=1163912552)"
" (DH) and "
"[DSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" protocols involve the generation of public keys of the form $ y = "
"g^{x}~mod~p$, where the private key $x$ is the discrete logarithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua protokol [Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman_key_exchange&oldid=1163912552)"
" (DH) dan "
"[DSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" melibatkan pembuatan kunci publik dalam bentuk $ y = g^{x}~mod~p$, di mana "
"kunci privat $x$ adalah logaritma diskret.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An attacker who can solve an instance of the DLP can expose the private key "
"of one of the two parties and, by combining it with the public key of the "
"second party, get access to the shared secret. In the case of DSA, an "
"attacker who can solve the DLP can recover the signer's private key, voiding"
" the basic premise of a digital signature.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penyerang yang dapat memecahkan sebuah contoh DLP dapat mengekspos kunci "
"privat salah satu dari dua pihak dan, dengan menggabungkannya dengan kunci "
"publik pihak kedua, mendapatkan akses ke rahasia bersama. Dalam kasus DSA, "
"penyerang yang dapat memecahkan DLP dapat memulihkan kunci privat penanda "
"tangan, membatalkan premis dasar dari tanda tangan digital.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On classical computing systems, the DLP is believed not to have a "
"polynomial-time solution. But as shown by Peter Shor in his [original 1994 "
"paper](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700), Shor's algorithm also "
"solves the DLP in polynomial-time on quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada sistem komputasi klasik, DLP diyakini tidak memiliki solusi waktu "
"polinomial. Namun seperti yang ditunjukkan oleh Peter Shor dalam [makalah "
"aslinya tahun 1994](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700), algoritma "
"Shor juga memecahkan DLP dalam waktu polinomial pada komputer kuantum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor's algorithm and the discrete logarithm problem {#shors-algorithm-and-"
"the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Shor dan masalah logaritma diskret {#shors-algorithm-and-the-"
"discrete-logarithm-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor's algorithm is able to solve the discrete logarithm problem in "
"polynomial time. It primarily achieves its efficiency by using quantum "
"algorithms which can find the period of a function which depends on the "
"input to the problem - which is then combined with more conventional "
"operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Shor mampu memecahkan masalah logaritma diskret dalam waktu "
"polinomial. Efisiensinya terutama dicapai dengan menggunakan algoritma "
"kuantum yang dapat menemukan periode dari sebuah fungsi yang bergantung pada"
" input masalah — yang kemudian digabungkan dengan operasi yang lebih "
"konvensional.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of Shor's algorithm\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Detail matematis algoritma Shor\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor's algorithm provides an efficient solution to the DLP by mapping it to "
"a more general problem in group theory known as the [hidden subgroup "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hidden_subgroup_problem)"
" (HSP).\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Shor menyediakan solusi yang efisien untuk DLP dengan memetakannya"
" ke masalah yang lebih umum dalam teori grup yang dikenal sebagai [masalah "
"subgrup "
"tersembunyi](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hidden_subgroup_problem)"
" (HSP).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the HSP, one is given an algebraic group $G$ and a function $f: G "
"\\rightarrow X$  from $G$ to some set $X$ such that $f$ is constant on each "
"coset of some subgroup $H$ of $G$ (and distinct on different cosets). Then, "
"the task is to determine $H$. It is known that quantum computers can solve "
"the HSP on finite Abelian groups in time polynomial in $log~|G|$ where $|G|$"
" is the group order.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam HSP, seseorang diberikan grup aljabar $G$ dan fungsi $f: G "
"\\rightarrow X$  dari $G$ ke beberapa himpunan $X$ sedemikian sehingga $f$ "
"konstan pada setiap koset dari beberapa subgrup $H$ dari $G$ (dan berbeda "
"pada koset yang berbeda). Kemudian, tugasnya adalah menentukan $H$. "
"Diketahui bahwa komputer kuantum dapat memecahkan HSP pada grup Abel hingga "
"dalam waktu polinomial dalam $log~|G|$ di mana $|G|$ adalah orde grup.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the case of the integer DLP discussed in this lesson, the mapping to the "
"HSP is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kasus DLP integer yang dibahas dalam pelajaran ini, pemetaan ke HSP "
"adalah sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let $p$ be a prime and consider the DLP given by $ y = g^r~mod~p$ where $g$ "
"is a generator of $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$. Since $g^{p-1} \\equiv "
"1~mod~p$, $g$ has order $p-1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalkan $p$ adalah sebuah prima dan pertimbangkan DLP yang diberikan oleh $"
" y = g^r~mod~p$ di mana $g$ adalah generator dari "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$. Karena $g^{p-1} \\equiv 1~mod~p$, $g$ berorde "
"$p-1$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose $G = \\mathbb{Z}_{p-1} \\times \\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}$ where "
"$\\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}$ is the group of integers modulo $(p-1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih $G = \\mathbb{Z}_{p-1} \\times \\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}$ di mana "
"$\\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}$ adalah grup bilangan bulat modulo $(p-1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose $f : G \\rightarrow (\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ given as $f(a, b) = "
"g^a y^{-b}~mod~p \\equiv g^{a-rb}~mod~p$ .\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih $f : G \\rightarrow (\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ yang diberikan sebagai "
"$f(a, b) = g^a y^{-b}~mod~p \\equiv g^{a-rb}~mod~p$ .\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The kernel of $f$ is then the subgroup $H_0 = \\langle (r, 1) \\rangle = "
"\\{(a,b) \\in G | f(a,b) \\equiv 1~mod~p\\} = \\{ (a, b) \\in G | a - rb "
"\\equiv 0~mod~(p-1)\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kernel dari $f$ kemudian merupakan subgrup $H_0 = \\langle (r, 1) \\rangle ="
" \\{(a,b) \\in G | f(a,b) \\equiv 1~mod~p\\} = \\{ (a, b) \\in G | a - rb "
"\\equiv 0~mod~(p-1)\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$f$ is constant on the cosets $(\\delta, 0) + H_0$ and \"hides\" the "
"subgroup $H_0$ setting up an HSP.\n"
msgstr ""
"$f$ konstan pada koset $(\\delta, 0) + H_0$ dan \"menyembunyikan\" subgrup "
"$H_0$ yang membentuk HSP.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the above, Shor's quantum algorithm for the integer DLP uses a quantum"
" oracle to evaluate the function $f$ on a state representing a uniform "
"superposition over $G$, and then uses the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A "
"quantum algorithm that can be used to find periodic patterns. Named after "
"the Fourier transform in classical physics which can split a signal into a "
"set of sine waves.\">quantum Fourier transform</DefinitionTooltip> and "
"measurements with <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum algorithm used "
"to estimate phase in qubits, named after phase estimation in classical "
"physics.\">phase estimation</DefinitionTooltip> to produce quantum states "
"that allow for the identification of the generator $(r, 1)$ of $H_0$. From "
"this, $r$, the discrete logarithm of interest, can be extracted.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengingat hal di atas, algoritma kuantum Shor untuk DLP integer menggunakan "
"oracle kuantum untuk mengevaluasi fungsi $f$ pada keadaan yang "
"merepresentasikan superposisi seragam atas $G$, kemudian menggunakan "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum algorithm that can be used to find"
" periodic patterns. Named after the Fourier transform in classical physics "
"which can split a signal into a set of sine waves.\">transformasi Fourier "
"kuantum</DefinitionTooltip> dan pengukuran dengan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A quantum algorithm used to estimate phase in qubits, named "
"after phase estimation in classical physics.\">estimasi "
"fase</DefinitionTooltip> untuk menghasilkan keadaan kuantum yang "
"memungkinkan identifikasi generator $(r, 1)$ dari $H_0$. Dari sini, $r$, "
"logaritma diskret yang menjadi perhatian, dapat diekstrak.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Shor's original paper](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) has a "
"detailed description of the algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Makalah asli Shor](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) memiliki "
"deskripsi terperinci tentang algoritmanya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Elliptic curve cryptography {#elliptic-curve-cryptography}"
msgstr "Kriptografi kurva eliptik {#elliptic-curve-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[*Elliptic curve cryptography "
"(ECC)*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_cryptography&oldid=1160709993), based on the mathematics of [*elliptic"
" "
"curves*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve&oldid=1164567664),"
" offers a powerful approach to asymmetric key cryptography. ECC is known to "
"provide a similar level of security as methods such as RSA but with shorter "
"keys, making it more efficient and particularly well suited to systems with "
"limited resources, such as embedded systems and mobile devices, where the "
"[storage and computational savings of smaller key sizes are highly "
"desirable](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2881444).\n"
msgstr ""
"[*Kriptografi kurva eliptik "
"(ECC)*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_cryptography&oldid=1160709993), yang didasarkan pada matematika "
"[*kurva "
"eliptik*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve&oldid=1164567664),"
" menawarkan pendekatan yang kuat untuk kriptografi kunci asimetris. ECC "
"dikenal bisa memberikan tingkat keamanan yang serupa dengan metode seperti "
"RSA tetapi dengan kunci yang lebih pendek, sehingga lebih efisien dan sangat"
" cocok untuk sistem dengan sumber daya terbatas, seperti sistem tertanam dan"
" perangkat mobile, di mana [penghematan penyimpanan dan komputasi dari "
"ukuran kunci yang lebih kecil sangat "
"diinginkan](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2881444).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Basic principles of elliptic curve cryptography {#basic-principles-of-"
"elliptic-curve-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Prinsip dasar kriptografi kurva eliptik {#basic-principles-of-elliptic-"
"curve-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An elliptic curve is typically of the form $y^2 = x^3 + ax + b$ with a few interesting properties.\n"
"* It is horizontally symmetric. So for any point $(x,y)$ on the curve, it's reflection $(x,-y)$ is also on the curve\n"
"* Any non-vertical strain line will only intersect the curve at a maximum of three points\n"
msgstr ""
"Kurva eliptik umumnya berbentuk $y^2 = x^3 + ax + b$ dengan beberapa sifat menarik.\n"
"* Kurva ini simetris secara horizontal. Jadi untuk setiap titik $(x,y)$ pada kurva, refleksinya $(x,-y)$ juga ada pada kurva\n"
"* Setiap garis lurus non-vertikal hanya akan memotong kurva di maksimal tiga titik\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 1. Operations of addition and point doubling on an elliptic curve. "
"Facet 1 defines <b>P + Q = -R</b>. Facet 2 illustrates point doubling <b>2Q "
"= -P</b>. Facet 3 defines the additive inverse of a point as its reflection "
"about the x-axis i.e, <b>P = -Q</b> ](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/ECCfig.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 1. Operations of addition and point doubling on an elliptic curve. "
"Facet 1 defines <b>P + Q = -R</b>. Facet 2 illustrates point doubling <b>2Q "
"= -P</b>. Facet 3 defines the additive inverse of a point as its reflection "
"about the x-axis i.e, <b>P = -Q</b> ](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/ECCfig.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 1. Operations of addition and point doubling on an elliptic curve. "
"Facet 1 defines <b>P + Q = -R</b>. Facet 2 illustrates point doubling <b>2Q "
"= -P</b>. Facet 3 defines the additive inverse of a point as its reflection "
"about the x-axis i.e, <b>P = -Q</b>*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Gambar 1. Operasi penjumlahan dan penggandaan titik pada kurva eliptik. "
"Sisi 1 mendefinisikan <b>P + Q = -R</b>. Sisi 2 mengilustrasikan penggandaan"
" titik <b>2Q = -P</b>. Sisi 3 mendefinisikan invers aditif dari suatu titik "
"sebagai refleksinya terhadap sumbu x, yaitu <b>P = -Q</b>*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elliptic curve cryptography makes use of applying a series of arithmetic "
"operations to points on the curve. Each effectively navigates to a new point"
" on the curve. This is a simple process to follow in one direction, and with"
" shorter key sizes is more efficient than other algorithms like RSA, but "
"trying to reverse this is very difficult, hence its application to "
"cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kriptografi kurva eliptik memanfaatkan serangkaian operasi aritmatika pada "
"titik-titik di kurva. Setiap operasi secara efektif menavigasi ke titik baru"
" pada kurva. Ini adalah proses yang mudah diikuti dalam satu arah, dan "
"dengan ukuran kunci yang lebih pendek lebih efisien dari algoritma lain "
"seperti RSA, tetapi mencoba membalikkannya sangat sulit, sehingga bisa "
"diaplikasikan untuk kriptografi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical principles of elliptic curve cryptography\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Prinsip matematis kriptografi kurva eliptik\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An [elliptic "
"curve](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve&oldid=1164567664)"
" over an algebraic field $K$ is defined by a mathematical equation, "
"typically in the form $y^2 = x^3 + ax + b$ with the coefficients $a, b \\in "
"K$ and describes points $(x, y) \\in K \\otimes K$ with the additional "
"requirement that the curve have no kinks or self-intersections.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebuah [kurva "
"eliptik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve&oldid=1164567664)"
" di atas medan aljabar $K$ didefinisikan oleh persamaan matematika, umumnya "
"berbentuk $y^2 = x^3 + ax + b$ dengan koefisien $a, b \\in K$ dan "
"mendeskripsikan titik-titik $(x, y) \\in K \\otimes K$ dengan persyaratan "
"tambahan bahwa kurva tidak memiliki kink atau perpotongan diri.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The properties of elliptic curves allow for operations of \"addition\" and "
"\"scalar multiplication\" to be defined involving points on the curve.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sifat-sifat kurva eliptik memungkinkan operasi \"penjumlahan\" dan "
"\"perkalian skalar\" didefinisikan melibatkan titik-titik pada kurva.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Addition**: If $P$ and $Q$ are two points on an elliptic curve, then $P + "
"Q$ describes a unique third point identified as follows: Draw the line that "
"intersects $P$ and $Q$ and find the third point, $R$, at which the line "
"intersects the curve again. We then define $P + Q =  −R$, the point opposite"
" $R$ reflected through the $x$-axis (see figure below) . When the line "
"through $P, Q$ does not intersect the curve at any finite $(x, y)$, we say "
"it intersects the curve at the point at infinity $\\mathbf{O}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Penjumlahan**: Jika $P$ dan $Q$ adalah dua titik pada kurva eliptik, maka "
"$P + Q$ mendeskripsikan titik ketiga yang unik yang diidentifikasi sebagai "
"berikut: Tarik garis yang memotong $P$ dan $Q$ dan temukan titik ketiga, "
"$R$, di mana garis tersebut memotong kurva lagi. Kita kemudian "
"mendefinisikan $P + Q =  −R$, titik yang berlawanan dari $R$ yang "
"dicerminkan melalui sumbu $x$ (lihat gambar di bawah). Ketika garis melalui "
"$P, Q$ tidak memotong kurva di $(x, y)$ yang berhingga, kita katakan ia "
"memotong kurva di titik tak hingga $\\mathbf{O}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elliptic curve addition satisfies algebraic **group** properties with the "
"point at infinity as the additive identity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penjumlahan kurva eliptik memenuhi sifat **grup** aljabar dengan titik tak "
"hingga sebagai identitas aditif.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Doubling and scalar multiplication:** The operation of point doubling "
"which corresponds to scalar multiplication by $2$ is obtained by setting $P "
"= Q$ in the addition operation and graphically involves the tangent line at "
"$P$. General scalar multiplication by an integer $n$ defined as $nP =  P + P"
" + ...~n$ times is obtained by repeated doubling and addition.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Penggandaan dan perkalian skalar:** Operasi penggandaan titik yang "
"bersesuaian dengan perkalian skalar oleh $2$ diperoleh dengan menetapkan $P "
"= Q$ dalam operasi penjumlahan dan secara grafis melibatkan garis singgung "
"di $P$. Perkalian skalar umum oleh bilangan bulat $n$ yang didefinisikan "
"sebagai $nP =  P + P + ...~n$ kali diperoleh dengan penggandaan dan "
"penjumlahan berulang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elliptic curve discrete logarithm problem {#elliptic-curve-discrete-"
"logarithm-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Masalah logaritma diskret kurva eliptik {#elliptic-curve-discrete-logarithm-"
"problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The elliptic curve discrete logarithm problem (ECDLP) has many similarities "
"to the discrete logarithm problem discussed previously, being based around "
"the challenges of finding factors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah logaritma diskret kurva eliptik (ECDLP) memiliki banyak kesamaan "
"dengan masalah logaritma diskret yang dibahas sebelumnya, yang didasarkan "
"pada tantangan menemukan faktor.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation of [scalar multiplication on elliptic "
"curves](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve_point_multiplication&oldid=1145917191)"
" allows for the definition of the [elliptic curve discrete logarithm "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_cryptography&oldid=1160709993):\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi [perkalian skalar pada kurva "
"eliptik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve_point_multiplication&oldid=1145917191)"
" memungkinkan definisi dari [masalah logaritma diskret kurva "
"eliptik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_cryptography&oldid=1160709993):\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given points $P, Q$ on an elliptic curve such that $Q = nP$, determine "
"$n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan titik $P, Q$ pada kurva eliptik sedemikian sehingga $Q = nP$, "
"tentukan $n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This problem is known to be intractable on classical computers for large $n$"
" and provides a basis for cryptographic security.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah ini diketahui tidak bisa diselesaikan pada komputer klasik untuk $n$"
" yang besar dan menjadi dasar keamanan kriptografi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of ECDLP\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Deskripsi matematis ECDLP\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elliptic curve cryptography is primarily based on the ECDLP formulated on "
"certain algebraic **finite fields**. In 1999, NIST recommended ten finite "
"fields for use in ECC. These are:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kriptografi kurva eliptik terutama didasarkan pada ECDLP yang dirumuskan "
"pada **medan hingga** aljabar tertentu. Pada tahun 1999, NIST "
"merekomendasikan sepuluh medan hingga untuk digunakan dalam ECC. Ini "
"adalah:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Five **prime fields** $\\mathbb {F} _{p}$ for primes $p$ of size $\\{192, "
"224, 256, 384, 521\\}$ bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lima **medan prima** $\\mathbb {F} _{p}$ untuk prima $p$ berukuran $\\{192, "
"224, 256, 384, 521\\}$ bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Five **binary fields** $\\mathbb {F} _{2^{n}}$ for $n \\in \\{163, 233, 283,"
" 409, 571\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lima **medan biner** $\\mathbb {F} _{2^{n}}$ untuk $n \\in \\{163, 233, 283,"
" 409, 571\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With the above setup, an ECC-based asymmetric key cryptosystem in the case "
"of **prime fields** may be specified as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan pengaturan di atas, sistem kriptografi kunci asimetris berbasis ECC "
"dalam kasus **medan prima** dapat ditentukan sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose a $p$ from the NIST-recommended list of values to specify $\\mathbb "
"{F} _{p}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih $p$ dari daftar nilai yang direkomendasikan NIST untuk menentukan "
"$\\mathbb {F} _{p}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Select parameters $a, b$ of the elliptic curve.\n"
msgstr "Pilih parameter $a, b$ dari kurva eliptik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose a **base point** $G$ which \"generates\" a cyclic subgroup on the "
"curve with order $n$; that is, the smallest integer such that $nG = "
"\\mathbf{O}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih **titik basis** $G$ yang \"menghasilkan\" subgrup siklik pada kurva "
"dengan orde $n$; yaitu, bilangan bulat terkecil sedemikian sehingga $nG = "
"\\mathbf{O}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calculate the **cofactor** $h = |E(\\mathbb {F} _{p})|/n$ where $|E(\\mathbb"
" {F} _{p})|$ is the number of points on the curve. $h$ is typically a small "
"integer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hitung **kofaktor** $h = |E(\\mathbb {F} _{p})|/n$ di mana $|E(\\mathbb {F} "
"_{p})|$ adalah jumlah titik pada kurva. $h$ biasanya merupakan bilangan "
"bulat kecil.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **domain parameters** $(p, a, b, G, n, h)$ allow the specification of "
"asymmetric keys in this way:\n"
msgstr ""
"**Parameter domain** $(p, a, b, G, n, h)$ memungkinkan spesifikasi kunci "
"asimetris dengan cara ini:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The private key is a randomly chosen integer $d$ with as many bits as in the"
" prime $p$. It should be kept secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci privat adalah bilangan bulat yang dipilih secara acak $d$ dengan bit "
"sebanyak prima $p$. Harus dijaga kerahasiaannya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The public key is the result of \"multiplying\" the base point $G$ by the "
"private key $d$. This is typically denoted as $Q = dG$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci publik adalah hasil \"mengalikan\" titik basis $G$ dengan kunci privat"
" $d$. Ini biasanya dinotasikan sebagai $Q = dG$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recovering $d$ is equivalent to solving the ECDLP, which is assumed to be "
"intractable for large $d$. The ECDLP therefore forms the basis for key "
"exchange and digital signature schemes in direct analogy with the Diffie-"
"Hellman and DSA schemes defined over $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ discussed "
"previously.\n"
msgstr ""
"Memulihkan $d$ setara dengan menyelesaikan ECDLP, yang diasumsikan tidak "
"bisa diselesaikan untuk $d$ yang besar. ECDLP oleh karena itu membentuk "
"dasar untuk pertukaran kunci dan skema tanda tangan digital secara analogi "
"langsung dengan skema Diffie-Hellman dan DSA yang didefinisikan di atas "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ yang dibahas sebelumnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Key exchange with ECC {#key-exchange-with-ecc}"
msgstr "Pertukaran kunci dengan ECC {#key-exchange-with-ecc}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One of the primary uses of ECC is in the key exchange protocol known as "
"[elliptic curve Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman&oldid=1160050860) (ECDH). In ECDH, each party "
"generates a private-public key pair and then exchanges public keys. Each "
"party then uses their own private key and the other party's public key to "
"compute a shared secret, which can be used as the key for symmetric "
"encryption.\n"
msgstr ""
"Salah satu penggunaan utama ECC adalah dalam protokol pertukaran kunci yang "
"dikenal sebagai [Diffie-Hellman kurva "
"eliptik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman&oldid=1160050860) (ECDH). Dalam ECDH, setiap "
"pihak menghasilkan pasangan kunci privat-publik dan kemudian menukar kunci "
"publik. Setiap pihak kemudian menggunakan kunci privat mereka sendiri dan "
"kunci publik pihak lain untuk menghitung rahasia bersama, yang dapat "
"digunakan sebagai kunci untuk enkripsi simetris.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While it's relatively easy to perform point addition on an elliptic curve "
"and derive a public key from a private key, it's computationally infeasible "
"to reverse the process and derive a private key from a public key. This "
"\"one-way\" behavior provides the security of the ECDH key exchange.\n"
msgstr ""
"Meskipun relatif mudah untuk melakukan penjumlahan titik pada kurva eliptik "
"dan mendapatkan kunci publik dari kunci privat, secara komputasional tidak "
"memungkinkan untuk membalikkan proses dan mendapatkan kunci privat dari "
"kunci publik. Perilaku \"satu arah\" ini memberikan keamanan pertukaran "
"kunci ECDH.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we will illustrate an example of how one might perform an ECDH key "
"exchange using Python and the library `cryptography`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, kita akan mengilustrasikan contoh bagaimana seseorang mungkin "
"melakukan pertukaran kunci ECDH menggunakan Python dan library "
"`cryptography`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Digital signatures with ECC {#digital-signatures-with-ecc}"
msgstr "Tanda tangan digital dengan ECC {#digital-signatures-with-ecc}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ECC can also be used to generate digital signatures using the [Elliptic "
"Curve Digital Signature "
"Algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_Curve_Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1162097661)"
" (ECDSA). In ECDSA, the signer creates a signature using their private key, "
"and others can verify the signature using the signer's public key. Just like"
" with ECDH, the security of ECDSA relies on the ECDLP. It's computationally "
"infeasible for someone to forge a signature without access to the signer's "
"private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"ECC juga bisa digunakan untuk menghasilkan tanda tangan digital menggunakan "
"[Algoritma Tanda Tangan Digital Kurva "
"Eliptik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_Curve_Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1162097661)"
" (ECDSA). Dalam ECDSA, penandatangan membuat tanda tangan menggunakan kunci "
"privat mereka, dan orang lain bisa memverifikasi tanda tangan menggunakan "
"kunci publik penandatangan. Sama seperti dengan ECDH, keamanan ECDSA "
"bergantung pada ECDLP. Secara komputasional tidak memungkinkan bagi "
"seseorang untuk memalsukan tanda tangan tanpa akses ke kunci privat "
"penandatangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following is an example of a simple sign-and-verify transaction using "
"ECDSA with Python and `cryptography`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah contoh transaksi tanda-dan-verifikasi sederhana menggunakan "
"ECDSA dengan Python dan `cryptography`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above code, if one modifies the message after it has been signed, the"
" verification will fail, providing a guarantee of authenticity and integrity"
" for the message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kode di atas, jika seseorang memodifikasi pesan setelah "
"ditandatangani, verifikasi akan gagal, memberikan jaminan keaslian dan "
"integritas untuk pesan tersebut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Breaking ECDH and ECDSA {#breaking-ecdh-and-ecdsa}"
msgstr "Membobol ECDH dan ECDSA {#breaking-ecdh-and-ecdsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In an analogous way to the integer discrete logarithm problem, the ECDLP "
"turns out to be hard on classical computers but has an efficient solution on"
" quantum computers once again via Shor's algorithm. We refer you to recent "
"literature for a discussion related to [generalizing Shor's algorithm to the"
" ECDLP case](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-89432-0_8).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan cara yang analog dengan masalah logaritma diskret bilangan bulat, "
"ECDLP ternyata sulit pada komputer klasik tetapi memiliki solusi yang "
"efisien pada komputer kuantum sekali lagi melalui algoritma Shor. Kami "
"merujuk kamu ke literatur terbaru untuk diskusi terkait [generalisasi "
"algoritma Shor ke kasus "
"ECDLP](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-89432-0_8).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Ringkasan {#summary}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson, we started by looking at the main characteristics of "
"asymmetric key cryptography (AKC) and discussed basic security "
"considerations that underpin asymmetric cryptosystems. In particular, we "
"introduced the two main applications of AKC — namely, key exchange and "
"digital signatures — both of which are essential components of modern "
"internet-based communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran ini, kita mulai dengan melihat karakteristik utama "
"kriptografi kunci asimetris (AKC) dan mendiskusikan pertimbangan keamanan "
"dasar yang mendasari sistem kripto asimetris. Khususnya, kita memperkenalkan"
" dua aplikasi utama AKC — yaitu, pertukaran kunci dan tanda tangan digital —"
" yang keduanya merupakan komponen penting dalam komunikasi berbasis internet"
" modern.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We then looked at the RSA cryptosystem, which since the 1970s, has proven to"
" be of immense value for securing modern digital communications by enabling "
"key exchange and digital signatures within a simple and versatile framework."
" The cryptographic security of RSA with respect to classical computing is "
"based on the hardness of factoring large integers and requires key sizes in "
"the range of 2048 bits to assure the integers used in practical applications"
" are large enough to resist factorization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kemudian melihat sistem kriptografi RSA, yang sejak tahun 1970-an, "
"telah terbukti sangat berharga untuk mengamankan komunikasi digital modern "
"dengan memungkinkan pertukaran kunci dan tanda tangan digital dalam kerangka"
" yang sederhana dan serbaguna. Keamanan kriptografi RSA terhadap komputasi "
"klasik didasarkan pada kesulitan memfaktorkan bilangan bulat besar dan "
"membutuhkan ukuran kunci dalam kisaran 2048 bit untuk memastikan bilangan "
"bulat yang digunakan dalam aplikasi praktis cukup besar untuk menahan "
"faktorisasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We then looked at Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange and the Digital Signature"
" Algorithm (DSA). The security of these schemes is predicated on the integer"
" discrete logarithm (DLP) problem, the private key being computationally "
"hard to extract given the public key, with no polynomial time solution on "
"classical computers. Use of random and unique keys affords additional "
"security against attacks. Both the integer finite field and elliptic curve "
"variants of the DH and DSA protocols currently find widespread use across "
"many modern digital communications protocols such as "
"[*TLS*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531),"
" "
"[*SSH*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Secure_Shell&oldid=1158549718),"
" and so on.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kemudian melihat pertukaran kunci Diffie-Hellman (DH) dan Algoritma "
"Tanda Tangan Digital (DSA). Keamanan skema ini dipredikatkan pada masalah "
"logaritma diskret bilangan bulat (DLP), kunci privat yang secara "
"komputasional sulit diekstrak dari kunci publik, tanpa solusi waktu "
"polinomial pada komputer klasik. Penggunaan kunci acak dan unik memberikan "
"keamanan tambahan terhadap serangan. Baik varian medan hingga bilangan bulat"
" maupun kurva eliptik dari protokol DH dan DSA saat ini banyak digunakan di "
"berbagai protokol komunikasi digital modern seperti "
"[*TLS*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531),"
" "
"[*SSH*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Secure_Shell&oldid=1158549718),"
" dan sebagainya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally we looked at Elliptic curve cryptography. With its efficient key "
"size and strong security properties, it currently represents an excellent "
"choice for many cryptographic applications, from key exchange to digital "
"signatures.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terakhir, kita melihat kriptografi kurva eliptik. Dengan ukuran kunci yang "
"efisien dan sifat keamanan yang kuat, saat ini merupakan pilihan yang sangat"
" baik untuk banyak aplikasi kriptografi, dari pertukaran kunci hingga tanda "
"tangan digital.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All of these algorithms have exposure to attack from quantum algorithms, "
"since solutions can be developed to solve the mathematical problems which "
"acted as a premise in their design. One such example is Shor's algorithm. "
"Therefore they will need to be replaced by quantum-safe asymmetric "
"cryptosystems which are more resilient to attack from quantum - as well as "
"being as safe with classical algorithms. The mathematical problems they rely"
" on can be solved efficiently by quantum computers, necessitating the "
"development of quantum-safe asymmetric cryptosystems that can withstand "
"quantum attacks while maintaining classical security.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semua algoritma ini terpapar serangan dari algoritma kuantum, karena solusi "
"dapat dikembangkan untuk menyelesaikan masalah matematika yang menjadi "
"premis dalam desainnya. Salah satu contohnya adalah algoritma Shor. Oleh "
"karena itu, algoritma-algoritma ini perlu digantikan oleh sistem kripto "
"asimetris yang aman secara kuantum yang lebih tahan terhadap serangan dari "
"kuantum — sekaligus tetap aman dengan algoritma klasik. Masalah matematika "
"yang mereka andalkan dapat diselesaikan secara efisien oleh komputer "
"kuantum, sehingga memerlukan pengembangan sistem kripto asimetris yang aman "
"secara kuantum yang dapat menahan serangan kuantum sekaligus mempertahankan "
"keamanan klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A future lesson will look at quantum-safe cryptosystems and discuss the "
"required approach to maintain cryptographic security.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pelajaran mendatang akan melihat sistem kripto yang aman secara kuantum dan "
"mendiskusikan pendekatan yang diperlukan untuk mempertahankan keamanan "
"kriptografi.\n"
